{"meta": {"limit": 100, "next": "/api/v1/doc/document/?format=json&name__startswith=draft-ietf-tls&limit=100&offset=100", "offset": 0, "previous": null, "total_count": 113}, "objects": [{"abstract": "This document describes several cipher suites to be used with the \r\nTransport Layer Security (TLS) protocol.  Changes in US export\r\nregulations in 1999 permitted the export of software programs \r\nusing 56-bit data encryption and 1024-bit key exchange.  \r\nThe cipher suites described in this document were designed to take\r\nadvantage of this change in the regulations.", "ad": null, "expires": "2002-01-26T08:00:01Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 21183, "intended_std_level": null, "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-56-bit-ciphersuites", "note": "", "notify": "", "pages": 3, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-56-bit-ciphersuites/", "rev": "01", "rfc": null, "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": null, "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/2/", "/api/v1/doc/state/150/", "/api/v1/doc/state/38/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "submissions": [], "tags": [], "time": "2001-07-25T07:00:00Z", "title": "56-bit Export Cipher Suites For TLS", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": 595}, {"abstract": "   This document specifies a TLS 1.3 extension that allows TLS clients\n   and servers to authenticate with certificates and provide\n   confidentiality based on encryption with a symmetric key from the\n   usual key agreement algorithm and an external pre-shared key (PSK).\n   This Standards Track RFC (once approved) obsoletes RFC 8773, which\n   was an Experimental RFC.\n", "ad": "/api/v1/person/person/112723/", "expires": "2026-03-09T19:32:04Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 123312, "intended_std_level": "/api/v1/name/intendedstdlevelname/ps/", "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-8773bis", "note": "", "notify": "jsalowey@gmail.com", "pages": 16, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-8773bis/", "rev": "13", "rfc": null, "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": "/api/v1/person/email/jsalowey@gmail.com/", "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/3/", "/api/v1/doc/state/112/", "/api/v1/doc/state/7/", "/api/v1/doc/state/44/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "submissions": ["/api/v1/submit/submission/151756/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/153474/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/152446/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/152475/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/148200/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/138607/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/139245/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/143932/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/150305/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/154378/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/149436/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/155041/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/155063/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/155097/"], "tags": [], "time": "2026-07-15T23:37:48Z", "title": "TLS 1.3 Extension for Using Certificates with an External Pre-Shared Key", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "   Authorization support is required for various Internet\r\n   protocols, for example, TLS, CMS and their consumers,\r\n   and others. The X.509 AttributeCertificate provides a\r\n   structure which can form the basis for such services\r\n   [X.509]. This specification defines two profiles (a\r\n   simple one and a 'full' one)  for the use of X.509\r\n   AttributeCertificates to provide such authorization\r\n   services.\r\n", "ad": null, "expires": "1999-03-26T08:00:00Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 20601, "intended_std_level": null, "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-ac509prof", "note": "", "notify": "", "pages": 11, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-ac509prof/", "rev": "00", "rfc": null, "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": null, "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/2/", "/api/v1/doc/state/150/", "/api/v1/doc/state/38/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "submissions": [], "tags": [], "time": "1998-09-22T07:00:00Z", "title": "An Internet AttributeCertificate Profile for Authorization", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": 4417}, {"abstract": "This document describes a Transport Layer Security (TLS) extension for application-layer protocol negotiation within the TLS handshake.  For instances in which multiple application protocols are supported on the same TCP or UDP port, this extension allows the application layer to negotiate which protocol will be used within the TLS connection.", "ad": "/api/v1/person/person/19177/", "expires": "2014-09-04T08:47:49Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 20293, "intended_std_level": "/api/v1/name/intendedstdlevelname/ps/", "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-applayerprotoneg", "note": "", "notify": "", "pages": 9, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-applayerprotoneg/", "rev": "05", "rfc": null, "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": "/api/v1/person/email/joe@salowey.net/", "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/3/", "/api/v1/doc/state/108/", "/api/v1/doc/state/115/", "/api/v1/doc/state/7/", "/api/v1/doc/state/44/"], "std_level": "/api/v1/name/stdlevelname/ps/", "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "submissions": ["/api/v1/submit/submission/49801/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/50192/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/54203/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/54594/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/57132/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/58487/"], "tags": [], "time": "2017-11-03T07:19:21Z", "title": "Transport Layer Security (TLS) Application-Layer Protocol Negotiation Extension", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": 2025}, {"abstract": "   This document describes extensions to [TLS] providing\r\n   authorization support based on the use of X.509\r\n   AttributeCertificates.\r\n", "ad": null, "expires": "1999-03-26T08:00:01Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 20081, "intended_std_level": null, "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-attr-cert", "note": "", "notify": "", "pages": 11, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-attr-cert/", "rev": "01", "rfc": null, "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": null, "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/2/", "/api/v1/doc/state/150/", "/api/v1/doc/state/38/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "submissions": [], "tags": [], "time": "1998-09-22T07:00:00Z", "title": "TLS extensions for AttributeCertificate based authorization", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": 2220}, {"abstract": "   This document describes a mechanism for batch signing in TLS.\n", "ad": null, "expires": "2020-07-16T16:48:35Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 95053, "intended_std_level": null, "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-batch-signing", "note": "", "notify": "", "pages": 10, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-batch-signing/", "rev": "00", "rfc": null, "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": null, "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/2/", "/api/v1/doc/state/150/", "/api/v1/doc/state/40/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "submissions": ["/api/v1/submit/submission/109132/"], "tags": [], "time": "2022-11-10T11:07:24Z", "title": "Batch Signing for TLS", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "Transport Layer Security (TLS) handshakes often include fairly static information, such as the server certificate and a list of trusted certification authorities (CAs). This information can be of considerable size, particularly if the server certificate is bundled with a complete certificate chain (i.e., the certificates of intermediate CAs up to the root CA).\n\n This document defines an extension that allows a TLS client to inform a server of cached information, thereby enabling the server to omit already available information.", "ad": "/api/v1/person/person/19177/", "expires": "2016-11-12T19:26:56Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 37188, "intended_std_level": "/api/v1/name/intendedstdlevelname/ps/", "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-cached-info", "note": "", "notify": "", "pages": 19, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-cached-info/", "rev": "23", "rfc": null, "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": "/api/v1/person/email/joe@salowey.net/", "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/3/", "/api/v1/doc/state/108/", "/api/v1/doc/state/115/", "/api/v1/doc/state/7/", "/api/v1/doc/state/44/"], "std_level": "/api/v1/name/stdlevelname/ps/", "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "submissions": ["/api/v1/submit/submission/17887/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/21379/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/22970/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/22996/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/23037/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/23041/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/23306/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/25157/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/37651/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/37809/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/43273/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/44437/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/49636/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/54725/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/58092/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/64858/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/67404/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/67974/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/73491/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/74770/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/75364/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/78100/"], "tags": [], "time": "2018-12-20T08:30:37Z", "title": "Transport Layer Security (TLS) Cached Information Extension", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": 4779}, {"abstract": "This document proposes the addition of new cipher suites to the Transport Layer Security (TLS) protocol to support the Camellia encryption algorithm as a bulk cipher algorithm. [STANDARDS-TRACK]", "ad": "/api/v1/person/person/5376/", "expires": "2005-04-24T21:06:15Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 23125, "intended_std_level": "/api/v1/name/intendedstdlevelname/ps/", "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-camellia", "note": "", "notify": "shiho@rd.scei.sony.co.jp, <treese@acm.org>, ekr@rtfm.com", "pages": 7, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-camellia/", "rev": "06", "rfc": null, "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": null, "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/3/", "/api/v1/doc/state/7/"], "std_level": "/api/v1/name/stdlevelname/ps/", "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "submissions": [], "tags": ["/api/v1/name/doctagname/app-min/"], "time": "2015-10-14T20:50:06Z", "title": "Addition of Camellia Cipher Suites to Transport Layer Security (TLS)", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": 1461}, {"abstract": "   This draft defines a new TLS Certificate Compression scheme which\n   uses a shared dictionary of root and intermediate WebPKI\n   certificates.  The scheme smooths the transition to post-quantum\n   certificates by eliminating the root and intermediate certificates\n   from the TLS certificate chain without impacting trust negotiation.\n   It also delivers better compression than alternative proposals whilst\n   ensuring fair treatment for both CAs and website operators.  It may\n   also be useful in other applications which store certificate chains,\n   e.g.  Certificate Transparency logs.\n", "ad": null, "expires": "2025-03-20T09:41:56Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 120649, "intended_std_level": null, "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-cert-abridge", "note": "", "notify": "", "pages": 21, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-cert-abridge/", "rev": "02", "rfc": null, "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": null, "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/2/", "/api/v1/doc/state/150/", "/api/v1/doc/state/38/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "submissions": ["/api/v1/submit/submission/136475/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/141264/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/145637/"], "tags": [], "time": "2025-03-20T07:05:18Z", "title": "Abridged Compression for WebPKI Certificates", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "In TLS handshakes, certificate chains often take up the majority of the bytes transmitted.\n\n This document describes how certificate chains can be compressed to reduce the amount of data transmitted and avoid some round trips.", "ad": "/api/v1/person/person/115214/", "expires": "2020-07-09T21:36:56Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 77691, "intended_std_level": "/api/v1/name/intendedstdlevelname/ps/", "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-certificate-compression", "note": "", "notify": "Sean Turner <sean@sn3rd.com>", "pages": 8, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-certificate-compression/", "rev": "10", "rfc": null, "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": "/api/v1/person/email/sean@sn3rd.com/", "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/3/", "/api/v1/doc/state/108/", "/api/v1/doc/state/154/", "/api/v1/doc/state/112/", "/api/v1/doc/state/7/", "/api/v1/doc/state/44/"], "std_level": "/api/v1/name/stdlevelname/ps/", "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "submissions": ["/api/v1/submit/submission/87009/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/91608/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/92493/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/94947/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/98407/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/103069/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/108371/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/108414/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/108665/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/108816/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/108963/"], "tags": [], "time": "2020-12-02T07:34:02Z", "title": "TLS Certificate Compression", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": 1474}, {"abstract": "This document describes the use of the ChaCha stream cipher and Poly1305 authenticator in the Transport Layer Security (TLS) and Datagram Transport Layer Security (DTLS) protocols.\n\n This document updates RFCs 5246 and 6347.", "ad": "/api/v1/person/person/19177/", "expires": "2016-06-18T21:28:50Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 61398, "intended_std_level": "/api/v1/name/intendedstdlevelname/ps/", "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-chacha20-poly1305", "note": "", "notify": "\"Sean Turner\" <sean@sn3rd.com>", "pages": 8, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-chacha20-poly1305/", "rev": "04", "rfc": null, "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": "/api/v1/person/email/sean@sn3rd.com/", "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/3/", "/api/v1/doc/state/108/", "/api/v1/doc/state/112/", "/api/v1/doc/state/7/", "/api/v1/doc/state/44/"], "std_level": "/api/v1/name/stdlevelname/ps/", "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "submissions": ["/api/v1/submit/submission/69682/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/73840/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/73997/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/74354/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/74681/"], "tags": [], "time": "2018-12-20T08:30:33Z", "title": "ChaCha20-Poly1305 Cipher Suites for Transport Layer Security (TLS)", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": 1802}, {"abstract": "This document proposes several new ciphersuites.  At present, the symmetric ciphers supported by Transport Layer Security (TLS) are RC2, RC4, International Data Encryption Algorithm (IDEA), Data Encryption Standard (DES), and triple DES.  The protocol would be enhanced by the addition of Advanced Encryption Standard (AES) ciphersuites. [STANDARDS-TRACK]", "ad": null, "expires": "2002-07-18T07:00:06Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 23120, "intended_std_level": "/api/v1/name/intendedstdlevelname/ps/", "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-ciphersuite", "note": "", "notify": "", "pages": 7, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-ciphersuite/", "rev": "06", "rfc": null, "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": null, "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/3/", "/api/v1/doc/state/150/"], "std_level": "/api/v1/name/stdlevelname/ps/", "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "submissions": [], "tags": [], "time": "2013-03-02T16:57:24Z", "title": "Advanced Encryption Standard (AES) Ciphersuites for Transport Layer Security (TLS)", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": 1671}, {"abstract": "The Transport Layer Security (TLS) protocol (RFC 2246) includes features to negotiate selection of a lossless data compression method as part of the TLS Handshake Protocol and to then apply the algorithm associated with the selected method as part of the TLS Record Protocol.  TLS defines one standard compression method which specifies that data exchanged via the record protocol will not be compressed.  This document describes an additional compression method associated with a lossless data compression algorithm for use with TLS, and it describes a method for the specification of additional TLS compression methods. [STANDARDS-TRACK]", "ad": "/api/v1/person/person/5797/", "expires": "2004-07-19T07:00:07Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 26600, "intended_std_level": "/api/v1/name/intendedstdlevelname/ps/", "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-compression", "note": "", "notify": "<treese@acm.org>, <ekr@rtfm.com>", "pages": 8, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-compression/", "rev": "07", "rfc": null, "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": null, "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/3/", "/api/v1/doc/state/7/"], "std_level": "/api/v1/name/stdlevelname/ps/", "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "submissions": [], "tags": ["/api/v1/name/doctagname/app-min/"], "time": "2013-03-02T16:58:00Z", "title": "Transport Layer Security Protocol Compression Methods", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": 2295}, {"abstract": "   This document specifies a way for the parties in the Transport Layer\n   Security (TLS) protocol to indicate that an individual session ticket\n   can be used to perform resumption even if the Server Name of the new\n   connection does not match the Server Name of the original.\n", "ad": null, "expires": "2022-06-09T05:26:22Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 100067, "intended_std_level": null, "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-cross-sni-resumption", "note": "", "notify": "caw@heapingbits.net", "pages": 6, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-cross-sni-resumption/", "rev": "02", "rfc": null, "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": "/api/v1/person/email/caw@heapingbits.net/", "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/2/", "/api/v1/doc/state/150/", "/api/v1/doc/state/145/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "submissions": ["/api/v1/submit/submission/116338/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/119111/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/123036/"], "tags": [], "time": "2022-06-08T07:13:16Z", "title": "Transport Layer Security (TLS) Resumption across Server Names", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "   This document specifies a \"compact\" version of TLS 1.3 and DTLS 1.3.\n   It saves bandwidth by trimming obsolete material, tighter encoding, a\n   template-based specialization technique, and alternative\n   cryptographic techniques. cTLS is not directly interoperable with TLS\n   1.3 or DTLS 1.3 since the over-the-wire framing is different.  A\n   single server can, however, offer cTLS alongside TLS or DTLS.\n", "ad": null, "expires": "2024-10-19T12:45:11Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 96355, "intended_std_level": null, "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-ctls", "note": "", "notify": "caw@heapingbits.net", "pages": 26, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-ctls/", "rev": "10", "rfc": null, "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": "/api/v1/person/email/caw@heapingbits.net/", "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/2/", "/api/v1/doc/state/150/", "/api/v1/doc/state/38/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "submissions": ["/api/v1/submit/submission/111676/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/115590/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/118987/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/120391/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/122301/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/125068/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/127230/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/130758/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/132730/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/137928/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/141993/"], "tags": [], "time": "2024-10-19T07:05:01Z", "title": "Compact TLS 1.3", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "   This document describes the use of the Advanced Encryption Standard\r\n   (AES) Counter Mode for use as a Transport Layer Security (TLS) and\r\n   Datagram Transport Layer Security (DTLS) confidentiality mechanism.\r\n", "ad": null, "expires": "2006-12-18T08:00:01Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 32269, "intended_std_level": null, "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-ctr", "note": "", "notify": "", "pages": 10, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-ctr/", "rev": "01", "rfc": null, "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": null, "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/2/", "/api/v1/doc/state/150/", "/api/v1/doc/state/38/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "submissions": [], "tags": [], "time": "2006-06-16T07:00:00Z", "title": "AES Counter Mode Cipher Suites for TLS and DTLS", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": 2686}, {"abstract": "   This document specifies the use of Curve25519 and Curve448 for\n   ephemeral key exchange in the Transport Layer Security (TLS) and\n   Datagram TLS (DTLS) protocols.  It updates RFC 5246 (TLS 1.2) and RFC\n   4492 (Elliptic Curve Cryptography for TLS).\n", "ad": null, "expires": "2016-01-07T12:48:13Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 61408, "intended_std_level": null, "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-curve25519", "note": "", "notify": "", "pages": 11, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-curve25519/", "rev": "01", "rfc": null, "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": "/api/v1/person/email/joe@salowey.net/", "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/2/", "/api/v1/doc/state/150/", "/api/v1/doc/state/38/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "submissions": ["/api/v1/submit/submission/69622/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/70573/"], "tags": [], "time": "2016-01-07T08:10:27Z", "title": "Curve25519 and Curve448 for Transport Layer Security (TLS)", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": 2992}, {"abstract": "This document specifies a delegation protocol for use with the \r\nTransport Layer Security (TLS) protocol.  When the TLS session is \r\nusing X.509 certificates for authentication, then the delegation is \r\nof an X.509 Proxy Certificate, as defined in draft-ggf-x509-proxy.  \r\nWhen the TSL session is using Kerberos 5 for authentication, then \r\nthe delegation is of a Kerberos 5 forwardable ticket, as defined in \r\nRFC 1510.", "ad": null, "expires": "2002-01-13T08:00:01Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 24017, "intended_std_level": null, "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-delegation", "note": "", "notify": "", "pages": 10, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-delegation/", "rev": "01", "rfc": null, "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": null, "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/2/", "/api/v1/doc/state/150/", "/api/v1/doc/state/38/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "submissions": [], "tags": [], "time": "2001-07-12T07:00:00Z", "title": "TLS Delegation Protocol", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": 2128}, {"abstract": "   For (D)TLS 1.2, this document deprecates the use of two key\n   exchanges, namely Diffie-Hellman over a finite field and RSA, and it\n   discourages the use of static elliptic curve Diffie-Hellman cipher\n   suites.\n\n   These prescriptions apply only to (D)TLS 1.2 since (D)TLS 1.0 and TLS\n   1.1 are deprecated by RFC 8996 and (D)TLS 1.3 either does not use the\n   affected algorithms or does not share the relevant configuration\n   options.  (There is no DTLS version 1.1.)\n\n   This document updates RFCs 9325, 4346, 5246, 4162, 6347, 5932, 5288,\n   6209, 6367, 8422, 5289, 5469, 4785, 4279, 5487, 6655, and 7905, to\n   deprecate or discourage - i.e., change to MUST NOT or SHOULD NOT, as\n   listed in Section 5.3, Section 5.2, Section 5.3, Section 5.4, and\n   Section 5.5 - the use of cipher suites using the above key exchange\n   methods in (D)TLS 1.2 connections.\n", "ad": "/api/v1/person/person/112723/", "expires": "2026-07-16T17:28:09Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 108625, "intended_std_level": "/api/v1/name/intendedstdlevelname/ps/", "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-deprecate-obsolete-kex", "note": "", "notify": "joe@salowey.net", "pages": 23, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-deprecate-obsolete-kex/", "rev": "08", "rfc": null, "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": "/api/v1/person/email/joe@salowey.net/", "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/3/", "/api/v1/doc/state/108/", "/api/v1/doc/state/115/", "/api/v1/doc/state/7/", "/api/v1/doc/state/44/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "submissions": ["/api/v1/submit/submission/126656/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/130488/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/132790/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/136781/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/143419/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/145358/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/152923/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/157526/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/158700/"], "tags": [], "time": "2026-07-16T20:55:39Z", "title": "Deprecating Obsolete Key Exchange Methods in (D)TLS 1.2", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "Transport Layer Security (TLS) versions 1.0 (RFC 2246) and 1.1 (RFC 4346) include cipher suites based on DES (Data Encryption Standard) and IDEA (International Data Encryption Algorithm) algorithms.  DES (when used in single-DES mode) and IDEA are no longer recommended for general use in TLS, and have been removed from TLS version 1.2 (RFC 5246).  This document specifies these cipher suites for completeness and discusses reasons why their use is no longer recommended.  This memo provides information for the Internet community.", "ad": "/api/v1/person/person/19790/", "expires": "2008-12-27T08:00:02Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 35332, "intended_std_level": "/api/v1/name/intendedstdlevelname/inf/", "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-des-idea", "note": "", "notify": "", "pages": 4, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-des-idea/", "rev": "02", "rfc": null, "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": null, "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/3/", "/api/v1/doc/state/108/", "/api/v1/doc/state/7/"], "std_level": "/api/v1/name/stdlevelname/hist/", "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "submissions": ["/api/v1/submit/submission/4778/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/5920/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/7524/"], "tags": ["/api/v1/name/doctagname/app-min/"], "time": "2021-02-02T08:27:27Z", "title": "DES and IDEA Cipher Suites for Transport Layer Security (TLS)", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": 1088}, {"abstract": "   This draft describes a new TLS extension for transport of a DNS\n   record set serialized with the DNSSEC signatures needed to\n   authenticate that record set.  The intent of this proposal is to\n   allow TLS clients to perform DANE authentication of a TLS server\n   without needing to perform additional DNS record lookups.  It is not\n   intended to be used to validate the TLS server's address records.\n", "ad": "/api/v1/person/person/115214/", "expires": "2018-09-22T14:47:00Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 66459, "intended_std_level": "/api/v1/name/intendedstdlevelname/ps/", "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-dnssec-chain-extension", "note": "", "notify": "Joseph Salowey <joe@salowey.net>, shuque@gmail.com", "pages": 24, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-dnssec-chain-extension/", "rev": "07", "rfc": null, "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": "/api/v1/person/email/joe@salowey.net/", "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/4/", "/api/v1/doc/state/110/", "/api/v1/doc/state/115/", "/api/v1/doc/state/150/", "/api/v1/doc/state/38/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "submissions": ["/api/v1/submit/submission/78528/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/79523/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/83724/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/85681/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/86897/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/90554/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/92421/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/94341/"], "tags": [], "time": "2024-12-18T18:44:06Z", "title": "A DANE Record and DNSSEC Authentication Chain Extension for TLS", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": 6227}, {"abstract": "This document defines a Signaling Cipher Suite Value (SCSV) that prevents protocol downgrade attacks on the Transport Layer Security (TLS) and Datagram Transport Layer Security (DTLS) protocols.  It updates RFCs 2246, 4346, 4347, 5246, and 6347.  Server update considerations are included.", "ad": "/api/v1/person/person/19177/", "expires": "2015-08-23T22:51:18Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 55763, "intended_std_level": "/api/v1/name/intendedstdlevelname/ps/", "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-downgrade-scsv", "note": "", "notify": "", "pages": 8, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-downgrade-scsv/", "rev": "05", "rfc": null, "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": "/api/v1/person/email/turners@ieca.com/", "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/3/", "/api/v1/doc/state/108/", "/api/v1/doc/state/115/", "/api/v1/doc/state/7/", "/api/v1/doc/state/44/"], "std_level": "/api/v1/name/stdlevelname/ps/", "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "submissions": ["/api/v1/submit/submission/61665/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/64701/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/64808/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/65364/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/66632/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/66805/"], "tags": [], "time": "2022-04-06T07:48:43Z", "title": "TLS Fallback Signaling Cipher Suite Value (SCSV) for Preventing Protocol Downgrade Attacks", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": 2240}, {"abstract": "This document specifies the Connection ID (CID) construct for the Datagram Transport Layer Security (DTLS) protocol version 1.2.\n\n A CID is an identifier carried in the record layer header that gives the recipient additional information for selecting the appropriate security association. In \"classical\" DTLS, selecting a security association of an incoming DTLS record is accomplished with the help of the 5-tuple. If the source IP address and/or source port changes during the lifetime of an ongoing DTLS session, then the receiver will be unable to locate the correct security context.\n\n The new ciphertext record format with the CID also provides content type encryption and record layer padding.\n\n This document updates RFC 6347.", "ad": "/api/v1/person/person/115214/", "expires": "2021-12-24T22:22:11Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 82048, "intended_std_level": "/api/v1/name/intendedstdlevelname/ps/", "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-dtls-connection-id", "note": "", "notify": "Joseph Salowey <joe@salowey.net>", "pages": 14, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-dtls-connection-id/", "rev": "13", "rfc": null, "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": "/api/v1/person/email/joe@salowey.net/", "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/3/", "/api/v1/doc/state/108/", "/api/v1/doc/state/154/", "/api/v1/doc/state/112/", "/api/v1/doc/state/7/", "/api/v1/doc/state/44/"], "std_level": "/api/v1/name/stdlevelname/ps/", "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "submissions": ["/api/v1/submit/submission/91929/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/96618/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/99365/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/101609/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/102266/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/103589/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/105265/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/107144/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/115626/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/116829/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/117939/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/118656/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/119072/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/119804/"], "tags": [], "time": "2022-03-18T21:29:59Z", "title": "Connection Identifier for DTLS 1.2", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "This document describes the Heartbeat Extension for the Transport Layer Security (TLS) and Datagram Transport Layer Security (DTLS) protocols.\n\n The Heartbeat Extension provides a new protocol for TLS/DTLS allowing the usage of keep-alive functionality without performing a renegotiation and a basis for path MTU (PMTU) discovery for DTLS. [STANDARDS-TRACK]", "ad": "/api/v1/person/person/19483/", "expires": "2012-06-04T18:48:56Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 39025, "intended_std_level": "/api/v1/name/intendedstdlevelname/ps/", "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-dtls-heartbeat", "note": "Joe Salowey (jsalowey@cisco.com) is the document shepherd.", "notify": "", "pages": 9, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-dtls-heartbeat/", "rev": "04", "rfc": null, "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": null, "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/3/", "/api/v1/doc/state/108/", "/api/v1/doc/state/7/", "/api/v1/doc/state/44/"], "std_level": "/api/v1/name/stdlevelname/ps/", "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "submissions": ["/api/v1/submit/submission/24269/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/29740/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/34250/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/35666/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/37448/"], "tags": [], "time": "2022-02-01T08:44:04Z", "title": "Transport Layer Security (TLS) and Datagram Transport Layer Security (DTLS) Heartbeat Extension", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": 2247}, {"abstract": "   This document specifies a return routability check for use in context\n   of the Connection ID (CID) construct for the Datagram Transport Layer\n   Security (DTLS) protocol versions 1.2 and 1.3.\n\n   Implementations offering the CID functionality described in RFC 9146\n   and RFC 9147 are encouraged to also provide the return routability\n   check functionality described in this document.  For this reason,\n   this document updates RFC 9146 and RFC 9147.\n", "ad": "/api/v1/person/person/112723/", "expires": "2026-01-15T21:12:32Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 102454, "intended_std_level": "/api/v1/name/intendedstdlevelname/ps/", "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-dtls-rrc", "note": "", "notify": "sean@sn3rd.com", "pages": 23, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-dtls-rrc/", "rev": "20", "rfc": null, "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": "/api/v1/person/email/sean@sn3rd.com/", "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/3/", "/api/v1/doc/state/108/", "/api/v1/doc/state/154/", "/api/v1/doc/state/115/", "/api/v1/doc/state/7/", "/api/v1/doc/state/44/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "submissions": ["/api/v1/submit/submission/122293/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/119582/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/123253/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/123254/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/122934/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/124991/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/127055/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/128463/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/132011/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/136372/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/137140/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/141689/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/145784/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/150782/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/153601/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/152476/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/152661/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/152782/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/152898/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/153010/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/153981/"], "tags": [], "time": "2026-03-11T05:36:53Z", "title": "Return Routability Check for DTLS 1.2 and DTLS 1.3", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "This document specifies version 1.3 of the Datagram Transport Layer Security (DTLS) protocol. DTLS 1.3 allows client/server applications to communicate over the Internet in a way that is designed to prevent eavesdropping, tampering, and message forgery.\n\n The DTLS 1.3 protocol is based on the Transport Layer Security (TLS) 1.3 protocol and provides equivalent security guarantees with the exception of order protection / non-replayability. Datagram semantics of the underlying transport are preserved by the DTLS protocol.\n\n This document obsoletes RFC 6347.", "ad": "/api/v1/person/person/115214/", "expires": "2021-11-02T02:48:52Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 76901, "intended_std_level": "/api/v1/name/intendedstdlevelname/ps/", "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-dtls13", "note": "", "notify": "Sean Turner <sean@sn3rd.com>", "pages": 61, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-dtls13/", "rev": "43", "rfc": null, "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": "/api/v1/person/email/sean@sn3rd.com/", "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/3/", "/api/v1/doc/state/108/", "/api/v1/doc/state/115/", "/api/v1/doc/state/7/", "/api/v1/doc/state/44/"], "std_level": "/api/v1/name/stdlevelname/ps/", "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "submissions": ["/api/v1/submit/submission/99712/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/86254/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/88274/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/90516/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/91426/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/91427/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/91431/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/91432/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/91433/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/91434/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/91435/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/91436/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/91437/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/91439/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/91440/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/91441/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/91442/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/91443/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/91444/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/91445/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/91446/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/91447/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/91448/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/91449/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/93589/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/93587/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/93588/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/93592/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/96609/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/96611/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/99525/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/102744/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/105346/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/106959/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/108361/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/110301/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/110575/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/110597/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/112306/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/115661/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/116869/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/117174/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/118913/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/118781/"], "tags": [], "time": "2022-04-21T22:34:20Z", "title": "The Datagram Transport Layer Security (DTLS) Protocol Version 1.3", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": 9240}, {"abstract": "This document describes new key exchange algorithms based on Elliptic Curve Cryptography (ECC) for the Transport Layer Security (TLS) protocol.  In particular, it specifies the use of Elliptic Curve Diffie-Hellman (ECDH) key agreement in a TLS handshake and the use of Elliptic Curve Digital Signature Algorithm (ECDSA) as a new authentication mechanism.  This memo provides information for the Internet community.", "ad": "/api/v1/person/person/5376/", "expires": "2006-04-24T00:47:09Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 20204, "intended_std_level": "/api/v1/name/intendedstdlevelname/inf/", "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-ecc", "note": "", "notify": "ekr@networkresonance.com", "pages": 35, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-ecc/", "rev": "12", "rfc": null, "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": null, "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/3/", "/api/v1/doc/state/7/"], "std_level": "/api/v1/name/stdlevelname/inf/", "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "submissions": [], "tags": ["/api/v1/name/doctagname/app-min/"], "time": "2020-01-21T08:27:07Z", "title": "Elliptic Curve Cryptography (ECC) Cipher Suites for Transport Layer Security (TLS)", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": 8397}, {"abstract": "RFC 4492 describes elliptic curve cipher suites for Transport Layer Security (TLS).  However, all those cipher suites use HMAC-SHA-1 as their Message Authentication Code (MAC) algorithm.  This document describes sixteen new cipher suites for TLS that specify stronger MAC algorithms.  Eight use Hashed Message Authentication Code (HMAC) with SHA-256 or SHA-384, and eight use AES in Galois Counter Mode (GCM).  This memo provides information for the Internet community.", "ad": "/api/v1/person/person/106164/", "expires": "2008-11-10T08:00:07Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 34165, "intended_std_level": "/api/v1/name/intendedstdlevelname/inf/", "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-ecc-new-mac", "note": "", "notify": "", "pages": 6, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-ecc-new-mac/", "rev": "07", "rfc": null, "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": null, "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/3/", "/api/v1/doc/state/108/", "/api/v1/doc/state/7/"], "std_level": "/api/v1/name/stdlevelname/ps/", "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "submissions": ["/api/v1/submit/submission/4642/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/4694/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/6434/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/6626/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/6760/"], "tags": ["/api/v1/name/doctagname/app-min/"], "time": "2018-07-11T07:18:37Z", "title": "TLS Elliptic Curve Cipher Suites with SHA-256/384 and AES Galois Counter Mode (GCM)", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": 1577}, {"abstract": "   This draft defines three hybrid key agreement mechanisms for TLS 1.3\n   - X25519MLKEM768, SecP256r1MLKEM768, and SecP384r1MLKEM1024 - that\n   combine the post-quantum ML-KEM (Module-Lattice-Based Key\n   Encapsulation Mechanism) with an ECDHE (Elliptic Curve Diffie-\n   Hellman) exchange.\n", "ad": "/api/v1/person/person/112723/", "expires": "2026-11-27T16:24:16Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 145121, "intended_std_level": "/api/v1/name/intendedstdlevelname/ps/", "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-ecdhe-mlkem", "note": "", "notify": "joe@salowey.net", "pages": 12, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-ecdhe-mlkem/", "rev": "05", "rfc": null, "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": "/api/v1/person/email/joe@salowey.net/", "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/3/", "/api/v1/doc/state/108/", "/api/v1/doc/state/154/", "/api/v1/doc/state/112/", "/api/v1/doc/state/7/", "/api/v1/doc/state/44/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "submissions": ["/api/v1/submit/submission/150746/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/155629/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/157591/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/157692/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/159467/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/163593/"], "tags": [], "time": "2026-08-10T18:11:17Z", "title": "Post-quantum hybrid ECDHE-MLKEM Key Agreement for TLSv1.3", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "This document extends RFC 4279, RFC 4492, and RFC 4785 and specifies a set of cipher suites that use a pre-shared key (PSK) to authenticate an Elliptic Curve Diffie-Hellman exchange with Ephemeral keys (ECDHE).  These cipher suites provide Perfect Forward Secrecy (PFS).  This memo provides information for the Internet community.", "ad": "/api/v1/person/person/106164/", "expires": "2009-05-04T07:00:05Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 34286, "intended_std_level": "/api/v1/name/intendedstdlevelname/inf/", "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-ecdhe-psk", "note": "", "notify": "", "pages": 7, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-ecdhe-psk/", "rev": "05", "rfc": null, "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": null, "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/3/", "/api/v1/doc/state/108/", "/api/v1/doc/state/7/"], "std_level": "/api/v1/name/stdlevelname/inf/", "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "submissions": ["/api/v1/submit/submission/4494/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/9764/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/6280/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/8712/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/9474/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/10396/"], "tags": ["/api/v1/name/doctagname/app-min/"], "time": "2015-10-14T20:51:47Z", "title": "ECDHE_PSK Cipher Suites for Transport Layer Security (TLS)", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": 1583}, {"abstract": "This document defines several new cipher suites for version 1.2 of the Transport Layer Security (TLS) protocol and version 1.2 of the Datagram Transport Layer Security (DTLS) protocol.  These cipher suites are based on the Ephemeral Elliptic Curve Diffie-Hellman with Pre-Shared Key (ECDHE_PSK) key exchange together with the Authenticated Encryption with Associated Data (AEAD) algorithms AES-GCM and AES-CCM.  PSK provides light and efficient authentication, ECDHE provides forward secrecy, and AES-GCM and AES-CCM provide encryption and integrity protection.", "ad": "/api/v1/person/person/115214/", "expires": "2017-11-26T14:32:00Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 66416, "intended_std_level": "/api/v1/name/intendedstdlevelname/ps/", "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-ecdhe-psk-aead", "note": "", "notify": "Joseph Salowey <joe@salowey.net>", "pages": 7, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-ecdhe-psk-aead/", "rev": "05", "rfc": null, "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": "/api/v1/person/email/joe@salowey.net/", "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/3/", "/api/v1/doc/state/108/", "/api/v1/doc/state/112/", "/api/v1/doc/state/7/", "/api/v1/doc/state/44/"], "std_level": "/api/v1/name/stdlevelname/ps/", "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "submissions": ["/api/v1/submit/submission/78365/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/82690/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/85985/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/86385/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/86695/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/86805/"], "tags": [], "time": "2018-09-07T00:17:40Z", "title": "ECDHE_PSK with AES-GCM and AES-CCM Cipher Suites for TLS 1.2 and DTLS 1.2", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": 1727}, {"abstract": "   This document specifies an extension to the SSLKEYLOGFILE format to\n   support the logging of information about Encrypted Client Hello (ECH)\n   related secrets.  Two new labels are introduced, namely ECH_SECRET\n   and ECH_CONFIG, which log the Hybrid Public Key Encryption (HPKE)-\n   derived shared secret and the ECHConfig used for the ECH,\n   respectively.\n\n   This extension aims to facilitate debugging of TLS connections\n   employing ECH.\n", "ad": null, "expires": "2025-04-24T10:42:53Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 139533, "intended_std_level": "/api/v1/name/intendedstdlevelname/inf/", "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-ech-keylogfile", "note": "", "notify": "", "pages": 8, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-ech-keylogfile/", "rev": "01", "rfc": null, "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": null, "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/4/", "/api/v1/doc/state/150/", "/api/v1/doc/state/38/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "submissions": ["/api/v1/submit/submission/145986/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/146796/"], "tags": ["/api/v1/name/doctagname/rev-wglc/"], "time": "2024-12-05T03:10:08Z", "title": "SSLKEYLOGFILE Extension for Encrypted Client Hello (ECH)", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "This document is an update to the Transport Layer Security (TLS) \r\nExtensions.  This update provides an additional choice in the \r\nServerName type of the Server_Name extension.  The Server Name \r\nextension allows the client to specify the name of the server to \r\nwhich it is attempting to connect.  The new choice specified in this \r\ndocument allows the client to specify an email name as the server name. \r\n    ", "ad": null, "expires": "2004-05-27T07:00:00Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 28594, "intended_std_level": null, "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-emailaddr", "note": "", "notify": "", "pages": 4, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-emailaddr/", "rev": "00", "rfc": null, "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": null, "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/2/", "/api/v1/doc/state/150/", "/api/v1/doc/state/38/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "submissions": [], "tags": [], "time": "2003-11-24T08:00:00Z", "title": "Update to Transport Layer Security (TLS) Extensions", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": 694}, {"abstract": "This document describes a means of negotiating the use of the encrypt-then-MAC security mechanism in place of the existing MAC-then-encrypt mechanism in Transport Layer Security (TLS) and Datagram Transport Layer Security (DTLS).  The MAC-then-encrypt mechanism has been the subject of a number of security vulnerabilities over a period of many years.", "ad": "/api/v1/person/person/19177/", "expires": "2015-01-23T13:17:54Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 55063, "intended_std_level": "/api/v1/name/intendedstdlevelname/ps/", "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-encrypt-then-mac", "note": "", "notify": "", "pages": 7, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-encrypt-then-mac/", "rev": "03", "rfc": null, "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": "/api/v1/person/email/turners@ieca.com/", "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/3/", "/api/v1/doc/state/108/", "/api/v1/doc/state/112/", "/api/v1/doc/state/7/", "/api/v1/doc/state/44/"], "std_level": "/api/v1/name/stdlevelname/ps/", "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "submissions": ["/api/v1/submit/submission/58715/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/59691/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/60284/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/61896/"], "tags": [], "time": "2020-01-21T08:33:03Z", "title": "Encrypt-then-MAC for Transport Layer Security (TLS) and Datagram Transport Layer Security (DTLS)", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": 2171}, {"abstract": "   This document describes a mechanism in Transport Layer Security (TLS)\n   for encrypting a ClientHello message under a server public key.\n\nDiscussion Venues\n\n   This note is to be removed before publishing as an RFC.\n\n   Source for this draft and an issue tracker can be found at\n   https://github.com/tlswg/draft-ietf-tls-esni\n   (https://github.com/tlswg/draft-ietf-tls-esni).\n", "ad": "/api/v1/person/person/112723/", "expires": "2025-12-16T19:09:47Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 86686, "intended_std_level": "/api/v1/name/intendedstdlevelname/ps/", "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-esni", "note": "", "notify": "jsalowey@gmail.com", "pages": 53, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-esni/", "rev": "25", "rfc": null, "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": "/api/v1/person/email/jsalowey@gmail.com/", "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/3/", "/api/v1/doc/state/108/", "/api/v1/doc/state/154/", "/api/v1/doc/state/115/", "/api/v1/doc/state/7/", "/api/v1/doc/state/44/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "submissions": ["/api/v1/submit/submission/98005/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/98112/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/99256/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/102376/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/105392/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/108064/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/110787/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/112354/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/114931/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/116366/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/118024/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/119660/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/120040/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/120900/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/124117/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/128840/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/133093/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/137135/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/141021/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/149333/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/144829/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/144830/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/145629/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/145632/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/150719/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/152755/"], "tags": [], "time": "2026-03-04T05:51:53Z", "title": "TLS Encrypted Client Hello", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "This document describes a mechanism that builds on Transport Layer Security (TLS) or Datagram Transport Layer Security (DTLS) and enables peers to provide proof of ownership of an identity, such as an X.509 certificate.  This proof can be exported by one peer, transmitted out of band to the other peer, and verified by the receiving peer.", "ad": "/api/v1/person/person/112723/", "expires": "2022-09-05T20:42:14Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 77448, "intended_std_level": "/api/v1/name/intendedstdlevelname/ps/", "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-exported-authenticator", "note": "", "notify": "Sean Turner <sean@sn3rd.com>, Christopher Wood <christopherwood07@gmail.com>", "pages": 14, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-exported-authenticator/", "rev": "15", "rfc": null, "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": "/api/v1/person/email/sean@sn3rd.com/", "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/3/", "/api/v1/doc/state/108/", "/api/v1/doc/state/154/", "/api/v1/doc/state/112/", "/api/v1/doc/state/7/", "/api/v1/doc/state/44/"], "std_level": "/api/v1/name/stdlevelname/ps/", "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "submissions": ["/api/v1/submit/submission/86678/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/87271/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/87272/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/88277/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/93933/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/90890/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/91685/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/95676/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/98802/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/103556/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/108086/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/108762/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/112054/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/112788/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/116963/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/124619/"], "tags": [], "time": "2022-07-13T22:57:02Z", "title": "Exported Authenticators in TLS", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": 1569}, {"abstract": "   TLS 1.3 ensures forward secrecy by performing an ephemeral Diffie-\n   Hellman key exchange during the initial handshake, protecting past\n   communications even if a party's long-term keys (typically a private\n   key with a corresponding certificate) are later compromised.\n\n   While the built-in KeyUpdate mechanism allows application traffic\n   keys to be refreshed during a session, it does not incorporate fresh\n   entropy from a new key exchange and therefore does not provide post-\n   compromise security.  This limitation can pose a security risk in\n   long-lived sessions, such as those found in industrial IoT or\n   telecommunications environments.\n\n   To address this, this specification defines an extended key update\n   mechanism that performs a fresh execution of the key exchange\n   negotiated during the initial handshake within an active session,\n   thereby ensuring post-compromise security.\n\n   By forcing attackers to exfiltrate new key material repeatedly, this\n   approach mitigates the risks associated with static key compromise.\n   Regular renewal of session keys helps contain the impact of such\n   compromises.  The extension is applicable to both TLS 1.3 and DTLS\n   1.3.\n", "ad": null, "expires": "2027-01-05T16:05:54Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 139389, "intended_std_level": "/api/v1/name/intendedstdlevelname/ps/", "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-extended-key-update", "note": "", "notify": "", "pages": 43, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-extended-key-update/", "rev": "13", "rfc": null, "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": null, "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/1/", "/api/v1/doc/state/150/", "/api/v1/doc/state/38/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "submissions": ["/api/v1/submit/submission/145768/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/146638/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/146654/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/147075/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/149912/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/153815/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/156726/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/157056/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/158745/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/159846/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/160561/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/161222/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/161927/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/165584/"], "tags": [], "time": "2026-07-04T16:05:54Z", "title": "Extended Key Update for Transport Layer Security (TLS) 1.3", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "This document describes extensions that may be used to add functionality to Transport Layer Security (TLS).  It provides both generic extension mechanisms for the TLS handshake client and server hellos, and specific extensions using these generic mechanisms.  The extensions may be used by TLS clients and servers.  The extensions are backwards compatible - communication is possible between TLS 1.0 clients that support the extensions and TLS 1.0 servers that do not support the extensions, and vice versa. [STANDARDS-TRACK]", "ad": "/api/v1/person/person/5797/", "expires": "2003-08-14T07:00:06Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 24337, "intended_std_level": "/api/v1/name/intendedstdlevelname/ps/", "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-extensions", "note": "", "notify": "<treese@acm.org>", "pages": 29, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-extensions/", "rev": "06", "rfc": null, "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": null, "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/3/", "/api/v1/doc/state/7/"], "std_level": "/api/v1/name/stdlevelname/ps/", "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "submissions": [], "tags": ["/api/v1/name/doctagname/app-min/"], "time": "2013-03-02T16:57:48Z", "title": "Transport Layer Security (TLS) Extensions", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": 7752}, {"abstract": "This document provides usage guidance for external Pre-Shared Keys (PSKs) in Transport Layer Security (TLS) 1.3 as defined in RFC 8446.  It lists TLS security properties provided by PSKs under certain assumptions, then it demonstrates how violations of these assumptions lead to attacks.  Advice for applications to help meet these assumptions is provided.  This document also discusses PSK use cases and provisioning processes.  Finally, it lists the privacy and security properties that are not provided by TLS 1.3 when external PSKs are used.", "ad": "/api/v1/person/person/115214/", "expires": "2022-08-08T16:45:43Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 96836, "intended_std_level": "/api/v1/name/intendedstdlevelname/inf/", "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-external-psk-guidance", "note": "", "notify": "sean@sn3rd.com", "pages": 13, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-external-psk-guidance/", "rev": "06", "rfc": null, "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": "/api/v1/person/email/sean@sn3rd.com/", "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/3/", "/api/v1/doc/state/110/", "/api/v1/doc/state/113/", "/api/v1/doc/state/7/", "/api/v1/doc/state/44/"], "std_level": "/api/v1/name/stdlevelname/inf/", "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "submissions": ["/api/v1/submit/submission/112653/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/115675/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/117479/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/121828/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/123086/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/123486/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/123937/"], "tags": [], "time": "2023-09-19T07:16:03Z", "title": "Guidance for External Pre-Shared Key (PSK) Usage in TLS", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "This document describes an interface for importing external Pre-Shared Keys (PSKs) into TLS 1.3.", "ad": "/api/v1/person/person/105815/", "expires": "2022-10-24T15:22:18Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 88553, "intended_std_level": "/api/v1/name/intendedstdlevelname/ps/", "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-external-psk-importer", "note": "", "notify": "Joseph Salowey <joe@salowey.net>", "pages": 11, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-external-psk-importer/", "rev": "08", "rfc": null, "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": "/api/v1/person/email/joe@salowey.net/", "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/3/", "/api/v1/doc/state/108/", "/api/v1/doc/state/112/", "/api/v1/doc/state/7/", "/api/v1/doc/state/44/"], "std_level": "/api/v1/name/stdlevelname/ps/", "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "submissions": ["/api/v1/submit/submission/103743/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/106808/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/107878/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/109779/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/111380/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/112133/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/116160/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/124895/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/125852/"], "tags": [], "time": "2022-07-25T20:12:07Z", "title": "Importing External Pre-Shared Keys (PSKs) for TLS 1.3", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "A number of protocols wish to leverage Transport Layer Security (TLS) to perform key establishment but then use some of the keying material for their own purposes.  This document describes a general mechanism for allowing that. [STANDARDS-TRACK]", "ad": "/api/v1/person/person/106164/", "expires": "2010-03-11T23:03:40Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 33715, "intended_std_level": "/api/v1/name/intendedstdlevelname/ps/", "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-extractor", "note": "", "notify": "", "pages": 7, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-extractor/", "rev": "07", "rfc": null, "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": null, "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/3/", "/api/v1/doc/state/108/", "/api/v1/doc/state/7/"], "std_level": "/api/v1/name/stdlevelname/ps/", "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "submissions": ["/api/v1/submit/submission/5244/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/9270/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/10443/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/12904/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/13572/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/16644/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/17757/"], "tags": ["/api/v1/name/doctagname/app-min/"], "time": "2015-10-14T20:51:43Z", "title": "Keying Material Exporters for Transport Layer Security (TLS)", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": 2302}, {"abstract": "This document specifies an optional behavior of Transport Layer Security (TLS) client implementations, dubbed \"False Start\".  It affects only protocol timing, not on-the-wire protocol data, and can be implemented unilaterally.  A TLS False Start reduces handshake latency to one round trip.", "ad": "/api/v1/person/person/19177/", "expires": "2016-11-13T03:39:44Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 61046, "intended_std_level": "/api/v1/name/intendedstdlevelname/inf/", "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-falsestart", "note": "", "notify": "\"Sean Turner\" <sean@sn3rd.com>", "pages": 11, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-falsestart/", "rev": "02", "rfc": null, "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": "/api/v1/person/email/sean@sn3rd.com/", "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/3/", "/api/v1/doc/state/110/", "/api/v1/doc/state/113/", "/api/v1/doc/state/7/", "/api/v1/doc/state/44/"], "std_level": "/api/v1/name/stdlevelname/inf/", "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "submissions": ["/api/v1/submit/submission/68949/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/73830/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/78105/"], "tags": [], "time": "2016-08-10T22:05:38Z", "title": "Transport Layer Security (TLS) False Start", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": 3198}, {"abstract": "This document describes GREASE (Generate Random Extensions And Sustain Extensibility), a mechanism to prevent extensibility failures in the TLS ecosystem.  It reserves a set of TLS protocol values that may be advertised to ensure peers correctly handle unknown values.", "ad": "/api/v1/person/person/115214/", "expires": "2020-02-23T18:41:57Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 75229, "intended_std_level": "/api/v1/name/intendedstdlevelname/inf/", "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-grease", "note": "", "notify": "Sean Turner <sean@sn3rd.com>", "pages": 12, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-grease/", "rev": "04", "rfc": null, "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": "/api/v1/person/email/sean@sn3rd.com/", "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/3/", "/api/v1/doc/state/108/", "/api/v1/doc/state/112/", "/api/v1/doc/state/7/", "/api/v1/doc/state/44/"], "std_level": "/api/v1/name/stdlevelname/inf/", "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "submissions": ["/api/v1/submit/submission/83850/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/95698/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/100789/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/105793/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/106116/"], "tags": [], "time": "2020-03-09T22:15:38Z", "title": "Applying Generate Random Extensions And Sustain Extensibility (GREASE) to TLS Extensibility", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": 2124}, {"abstract": "This memo explains how to use the Upgrade mechanism in HTTP/1.1 to initiate Transport Layer Security (TLS) over an existing TCP connection. [STANDARDS-TRACK]", "ad": null, "expires": "2000-07-08T07:00:05Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 20754, "intended_std_level": "/api/v1/name/intendedstdlevelname/ps/", "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-http-upgrade", "note": "", "notify": "", "pages": 13, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-http-upgrade/", "rev": "05", "rfc": null, "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": null, "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/3/", "/api/v1/doc/state/150/"], "std_level": "/api/v1/name/stdlevelname/ps/", "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "submissions": [], "tags": [], "time": "2020-01-21T08:23:49Z", "title": "Upgrading to TLS Within HTTP/1.1", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": 4057}, {"abstract": "This memo describes how to use Transport Layer Security (TLS) to secure Hypertext Transfer Protocol (HTTP) connections over the Internet.  This memo provides information for the Internet community.", "ad": null, "expires": "2000-03-12T08:00:03Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 20007, "intended_std_level": "/api/v1/name/intendedstdlevelname/inf/", "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-https", "note": "", "notify": "", "pages": 7, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-https/", "rev": "03", "rfc": null, "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": null, "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/3/", "/api/v1/doc/state/150/"], "std_level": "/api/v1/name/stdlevelname/inf/", "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "submissions": [], "tags": [], "time": "2013-03-02T16:57:00Z", "title": "HTTP Over TLS", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": 2308}, {"abstract": "   Hybrid key exchange refers to using multiple key exchange algorithms\n   simultaneously and combining the result with the goal of providing\n   security even if a way is found to defeat the encryption for all but\n   one of the component algorithms.  It is motivated by transition to\n   post-quantum cryptography.  This document provides a construction for\n   hybrid key exchange in the Transport Layer Security (TLS) protocol\n   version 1.3.\n", "ad": "/api/v1/person/person/112723/", "expires": "2026-03-11T19:40:11Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 96148, "intended_std_level": "/api/v1/name/intendedstdlevelname/inf/", "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-hybrid-design", "note": "", "notify": "caw@heapingbits.net, durumcrustulum@gmail.com, joe@salowey.net", "pages": 23, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-hybrid-design/", "rev": "16", "rfc": null, "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": "/api/v1/person/email/joe@salowey.net/", "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/3/", "/api/v1/doc/state/108/", "/api/v1/doc/state/112/", "/api/v1/doc/state/7/", "/api/v1/doc/state/44/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "submissions": ["/api/v1/submit/submission/111515/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/114911/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/118659/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/120554/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/123491/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/128252/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/131786/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/136207/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/136205/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/136504/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/141778/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/146117/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/148526/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/152811/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/154148/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/155120/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/155027/"], "tags": [], "time": "2026-07-15T22:20:38Z", "title": "Hybrid key exchange in TLS 1.3", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "This document describes a number of changes to TLS and DTLS IANA registries that range from adding notes to the registry all the way to changing the registration policy. These changes were mostly motivated by WG review of the TLS- and DTLS-related registries undertaken as part of the TLS 1.3 development process.\n\n This document updates the following RFCs: 3749, 5077, 4680, 5246, 5705, 5878, 6520, and 7301.", "ad": "/api/v1/person/person/115214/", "expires": "2018-11-25T16:07:20Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 75107, "intended_std_level": "/api/v1/name/intendedstdlevelname/ps/", "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-iana-registry-updates", "note": "", "notify": "Stephen Farrell <stephen.farrell@cs.tcd.ie>", "pages": 20, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-iana-registry-updates/", "rev": "05", "rfc": null, "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": "/api/v1/person/email/stephen.farrell@cs.tcd.ie/", "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/3/", "/api/v1/doc/state/108/", "/api/v1/doc/state/112/", "/api/v1/doc/state/7/", "/api/v1/doc/state/44/"], "std_level": "/api/v1/name/stdlevelname/ps/", "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "submissions": ["/api/v1/submit/submission/83520/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/86239/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/90722/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/92005/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/92890/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/95432/"], "tags": [], "time": "2020-03-10T07:27:58Z", "title": "IANA Registry Updates for TLS and DTLS", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": 3502}, {"abstract": "   This document presents a number of problems encountered when\r\n   implementing TLS 1.0, TLS 1.1 and TLS Extensions for clients, and\r\n   their consequences.  The problems include servers that refuse to\r\n   connect with clients supporting newer versions of the protocol, or\r\n   that do not handle such negotiation properly.  Another problem\r\n   encountered is the incorrect use of values in the protocol messages.\r\n", "ad": null, "expires": "2007-04-21T07:00:00Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 33479, "intended_std_level": null, "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-interoperability", "note": "", "notify": "", "pages": 30, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-interoperability/", "rev": "00", "rfc": null, "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": null, "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/2/", "/api/v1/doc/state/150/", "/api/v1/doc/state/38/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "submissions": [], "tags": [], "time": "2006-10-18T07:00:00Z", "title": "Clientside interoperability experiences for the SSL and TLS protocols", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": 15102}, {"abstract": "RFC 2712 [KERBTLS] introduced mechanisms for supporting Kerberos \r\n[KERB] authentication within the TLS protocol [TLS].  This document \r\nextends RFC 2712 to support delegation of Kerberos credentials.  In \r\nthis way, a TLS server may obtain a Kerberos service ticket on behalf \r\nof the TLS client.  Thus, a single client identity may be used for \r\nauthentication within a multi-tier architecture.  This draft also \r\nproposes a mechanism for a TLS server to indicate Kerberos-specific \r\ninformation to the client within the certificate request message in \r\nthe initial exchange.", "ad": null, "expires": "2002-05-12T07:00:01Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 23242, "intended_std_level": null, "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-kerb", "note": "", "notify": "", "pages": 0, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-kerb/", "rev": "01", "rfc": null, "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": null, "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/2/", "/api/v1/doc/state/150/", "/api/v1/doc/state/38/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "submissions": [], "tags": [], "time": "2001-11-08T08:00:00Z", "title": "Kerberos Cipher Suites in Transport Layer Security (TLS)", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": 2930}, {"abstract": "This document proposes the addition of new cipher suites to the TLS protocol to support Kerberos-based authentication. [STANDARDS-TRACK]", "ad": null, "expires": "2000-03-05T08:00:04Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 18727, "intended_std_level": "/api/v1/name/intendedstdlevelname/ps/", "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-kerb-cipher-suites", "note": "", "notify": "", "pages": 7, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-kerb-cipher-suites/", "rev": "04", "rfc": null, "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": null, "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/3/", "/api/v1/doc/state/150/"], "std_level": "/api/v1/name/stdlevelname/ps/", "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "submissions": [], "tags": [], "time": "2018-07-21T07:22:17Z", "title": "Addition of Kerberos Cipher Suites to Transport Layer Security (TLS)", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": 1663}, {"abstract": "   This document defines a mechanism for servers to communicate\n   supported key share algorithms in DNS.  Clients may use this\n   information to reduce TLS handshake round-trips.\n", "ad": null, "expires": "2027-04-18T17:09:08Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 136345, "intended_std_level": null, "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-key-share-prediction", "note": "", "notify": "", "pages": 7, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-key-share-prediction/", "rev": "05", "rfc": null, "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": null, "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/1/", "/api/v1/doc/state/150/", "/api/v1/doc/state/38/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "submissions": ["/api/v1/submit/submission/170423/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/142894/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/145544/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/150275/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/154928/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/161378/"], "tags": [], "time": "2026-10-15T17:09:08Z", "title": "TLS Key Share Prediction", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "   A format that supports logging information about the secrets used in\n   a TLS connection is described.  Recording secrets to a file in\n   SSLKEYLOGFILE format allows diagnostic and logging tools that use\n   this file to decrypt messages exchanged by TLS endpoints.  This\n   format is intended for use in systems where TLS only protects test\n   data.\n", "ad": "/api/v1/person/person/112723/", "expires": "2025-12-11T08:25:10Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 132015, "intended_std_level": "/api/v1/name/intendedstdlevelname/inf/", "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-keylogfile", "note": "", "notify": "sean@sn3rd.com", "pages": 15, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-keylogfile/", "rev": "05", "rfc": null, "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": "/api/v1/person/email/sean@sn3rd.com/", "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/3/", "/api/v1/doc/state/108/", "/api/v1/doc/state/112/", "/api/v1/doc/state/7/", "/api/v1/doc/state/44/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "submissions": ["/api/v1/submit/submission/142276/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/139611/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/141713/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/148979/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/152618/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/151210/"], "tags": [], "time": "2026-07-15T23:37:41Z", "title": "The SSLKEYLOGFILE Format for TLS", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "The MD5 and SHA-1 hashing algorithms are increasingly vulnerable to attack, and this document deprecates their use in TLS 1.2 and DTLS 1.2 digital signatures.  However, this document does not deprecate SHA-1 with Hashed Message Authentication Code (HMAC), as used in record protection.  This document updates RFC 5246.", "ad": "/api/v1/person/person/105815/", "expires": "2022-03-24T15:23:46Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 92815, "intended_std_level": "/api/v1/name/intendedstdlevelname/ps/", "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-md5-sha1-deprecate", "note": "", "notify": "loganaden@gmail.com, sean@sn3rd.com", "pages": 5, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-md5-sha1-deprecate/", "rev": "09", "rfc": null, "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": "/api/v1/person/email/sean@sn3rd.com/", "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/3/", "/api/v1/doc/state/108/", "/api/v1/doc/state/154/", "/api/v1/doc/state/112/", "/api/v1/doc/state/7/", "/api/v1/doc/state/44/"], "std_level": "/api/v1/name/stdlevelname/ps/", "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "submissions": ["/api/v1/submit/submission/106241/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/109226/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/109355/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/112024/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/114819/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/118316/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/118404/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/119163/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/121244/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/121479/"], "tags": [], "time": "2021-12-20T17:24:20Z", "title": "Deprecating MD5 and SHA-1 Signature Hashes in TLS 1.2 and DTLS 1.2", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "This document proposes the addition of new cipher suites to the TLS\r\nprotocol version 1.0 to support the MISTY1 encryption algorithm as a\r\nbulk cipher algorithm.  Major change from the previous version is the\r\naddition of intellectual property section.\r\n", "ad": null, "expires": "2001-09-06T07:00:01Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 23112, "intended_std_level": null, "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-misty1", "note": "", "notify": "", "pages": 3, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-misty1/", "rev": "01", "rfc": null, "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": null, "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/2/", "/api/v1/doc/state/150/", "/api/v1/doc/state/38/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "submissions": [], "tags": [], "time": "2001-03-05T08:00:00Z", "title": "Addition of MISTY1 to TLS", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": 570}, {"abstract": "   This memo specifies how the post-quantum signature scheme ML-DSA\n   (FIPS 204) is used for authentication in TLS 1.3.\n", "ad": "/api/v1/person/person/123703/", "expires": "2027-03-15T17:01:23Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 146128, "intended_std_level": "/api/v1/name/intendedstdlevelname/inf/", "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-mldsa", "note": "", "notify": "sean@sn3rd.com", "pages": 6, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-mldsa/", "rev": "06", "rfc": null, "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": "/api/v1/person/email/sean@sn3rd.com/", "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/1/", "/api/v1/doc/state/108/", "/api/v1/doc/state/115/", "/api/v1/doc/state/17/", "/api/v1/doc/state/216/", "/api/v1/doc/state/44/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "submissions": ["/api/v1/submit/submission/152118/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/168917/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/155526/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/166178/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/161503/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/162924/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/164631/"], "tags": [], "time": "2026-10-12T15:28:14Z", "title": "Use of ML-DSA in TLS 1.3", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "   This memo defines ML-KEM-512, ML-KEM-768, and ML-KEM-1024 as\n   NamedGroups and registers IANA values in the TLS Supported Groups\n   registry for use in TLS 1.3 to achieve post-quantum (PQ) key\n   establishment.\n", "ad": "/api/v1/person/person/123703/", "expires": "2027-03-21T04:19:00Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 145737, "intended_std_level": "/api/v1/name/intendedstdlevelname/inf/", "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-mlkem", "note": "", "notify": "joe@salowey.net", "pages": 9, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-mlkem/", "rev": "11", "rfc": null, "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": "/api/v1/person/email/joe@salowey.net/", "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/1/", "/api/v1/doc/state/108/", "/api/v1/doc/state/112/", "/api/v1/doc/state/17/", "/api/v1/doc/state/216/", "/api/v1/doc/state/44/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "submissions": ["/api/v1/submit/submission/154197/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/154206/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/154211/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/151355/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/153970/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/157145/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/159633/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/159612/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/164881/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/168492/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/166639/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/169172/"], "tags": [], "time": "2026-10-12T16:38:10Z", "title": "ML-KEM Post-Quantum Key Agreement for TLS 1.3", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "This document defines the Transport Layer Security (TLS) Certificate Status Version 2 Extension to allow clients to specify and support several certificate status methods. (The use of the Certificate Status extension is commonly referred to as \"OCSP stapling\".) Also defined is a new method based on the Online Certificate Status Protocol (OCSP) that servers can use to provide status information about not only the server's own certificate but also the status of intermediate certificates in the chain.", "ad": "/api/v1/person/person/19483/", "expires": "2013-10-13T22:16:02Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 46345, "intended_std_level": "/api/v1/name/intendedstdlevelname/ps/", "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-multiple-cert-status-extension", "note": "Document Shepherd - Joe Salowey (jsalowey@cisco.com)", "notify": "", "pages": 10, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-multiple-cert-status-extension/", "rev": "08", "rfc": null, "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": null, "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/3/", "/api/v1/doc/state/108/", "/api/v1/doc/state/111/", "/api/v1/doc/state/7/", "/api/v1/doc/state/38/"], "std_level": "/api/v1/name/stdlevelname/ps/", "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "submissions": ["/api/v1/submit/submission/41243/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/42627/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/45623/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/48034/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/47415/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/49659/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/49740/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/49901/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/49905/"], "tags": [], "time": "2016-12-13T08:08:07Z", "title": "The Transport Layer Security (TLS) Multiple Certificate Status Request Extension", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": 2666}, {"abstract": "   Traditional discrete logarithm-based Diffie-Hellman (DH) key exchange\n   during the TLS handshake suffers from a number of security,\n   interoperability, and efficiency shortcomings.  These shortcomings\n   arise from lack of clarity about which DH group parameters TLS\n   servers should offer and clients should accept.  This document offers\n   a solution to these shortcomings for compatible peers by establishing\n   a registry of DH parameters with known structure and a mechanism for\n   peers to indicate support for these groups.\n", "ad": null, "expires": "2015-01-22T15:37:49Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 56187, "intended_std_level": null, "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-negotiated-dl-dhe", "note": "", "notify": "", "pages": 19, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-negotiated-dl-dhe/", "rev": "00", "rfc": null, "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": null, "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/4/", "/api/v1/doc/state/150/", "/api/v1/doc/state/38/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "submissions": ["/api/v1/submit/submission/61821/"], "tags": [], "time": "2015-03-13T21:08:31Z", "title": "Negotiated Discrete Log Diffie-Hellman Ephemeral Parameters for TLS", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": 5451}, {"abstract": "Traditional finite-field-based Diffie-Hellman (DH) key exchange during the Transport Layer Security (TLS) handshake suffers from a number of security, interoperability, and efficiency shortcomings. These shortcomings arise from lack of clarity about which DH group parameters TLS servers should offer and clients should accept. This document offers a solution to these shortcomings for compatible peers by using a section of the TLS \"Supported Groups Registry\" (renamed from \"EC Named Curve Registry\" by this document) to establish common finite field DH parameters with known structure and a mechanism for peers to negotiate support for these groups.\n\n This document updates TLS versions 1.0 (RFC 2246), 1.1 (RFC 4346), and 1.2 (RFC 5246), as well as the TLS Elliptic Curve Cryptography (ECC) extensions (RFC 4492).", "ad": "/api/v1/person/person/19177/", "expires": "2015-12-03T23:50:55Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 56492, "intended_std_level": "/api/v1/name/intendedstdlevelname/ps/", "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-negotiated-ff-dhe", "note": "", "notify": "", "pages": 29, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-negotiated-ff-dhe/", "rev": "10", "rfc": null, "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": "/api/v1/person/email/turners@ieca.com/", "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/3/", "/api/v1/doc/state/108/", "/api/v1/doc/state/115/", "/api/v1/doc/state/7/", "/api/v1/doc/state/44/"], "std_level": "/api/v1/name/stdlevelname/ps/", "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "submissions": ["/api/v1/submit/submission/67079/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/61919/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/62542/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/63472/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/64838/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/65214/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/65478/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/66997/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/68189/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/69036/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/69455/"], "tags": [], "time": "2018-12-20T08:30:36Z", "title": "Negotiated Finite Field Diffie-Hellman Ephemeral Parameters for Transport Layer Security (TLS)", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": 8247}, {"abstract": "This document defines a group of new TLS cipher suites that utilize \r\nthe NTRU encryption algorithm and the NSS signature algorithm.  \r\nThese cipher suites are designed to maximize computational \r\nefficiency on both the client and server sides and ease deployment \r\nof the TLS protocol on constrained and embedded devices.  The \r\ndocument assumes the reader is familiar with the TLS protocol.", "ad": null, "expires": "2002-01-07T08:00:00Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 24423, "intended_std_level": null, "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-ntru", "note": "", "notify": "", "pages": 15, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-ntru/", "rev": "00", "rfc": null, "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": null, "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/2/", "/api/v1/doc/state/150/", "/api/v1/doc/state/38/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "submissions": [], "tags": [], "time": "2001-07-06T07:00:00Z", "title": "NTRU Cipher Suites for TLS", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": 4318}, {"abstract": "This document formally deprecates Transport Layer Security (TLS) versions 1.0 (RFC 2246) and 1.1 (RFC 4346). Accordingly, those documents have been moved to Historic status. These versions lack support for current and recommended cryptographic algorithms and mechanisms, and various government and industry profiles of applications using TLS now mandate avoiding these old TLS versions. TLS version 1.2 became the recommended version for IETF protocols in 2008 (subsequently being obsoleted by TLS version 1.3 in 2018), providing sufficient time to transition away from older versions. Removing support for older versions from implementations reduces the attack surface, reduces opportunity for misconfiguration, and streamlines library and product maintenance.\n\n This document also deprecates Datagram TLS (DTLS) version 1.0 (RFC 4347) but not DTLS version 1.2, and there is no DTLS version 1.1.\n\n This document updates many RFCs that normatively refer to TLS version 1.0 or TLS version 1.1, as described herein. This document also updates the best practices for TLS usage in RFC 7525; hence, it is part of BCP 195.", "ad": "/api/v1/person/person/115214/", "expires": "2021-07-25T19:31:55Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 84814, "intended_std_level": "/api/v1/name/intendedstdlevelname/bcp/", "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-oldversions-deprecate", "note": "", "notify": "Sean Turner <sean@sn3rd.com>, Kathleen  Moriarty <kathleen.moriarty.ietf@gmail.com>", "pages": 18, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-oldversions-deprecate/", "rev": "12", "rfc": null, "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": "/api/v1/person/email/sean@sn3rd.com/", "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/3/", "/api/v1/doc/state/110/", "/api/v1/doc/state/113/", "/api/v1/doc/state/7/", "/api/v1/doc/state/44/"], "std_level": "/api/v1/name/stdlevelname/bcp/", "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "submissions": ["/api/v1/submit/submission/99763/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/98052/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/102074/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/102849/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/103687/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/104401/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/108948/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/114809/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/114884/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/115755/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/116312/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/116341/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/116887/"], "tags": [], "time": "2021-03-25T07:32:44Z", "title": "Deprecating TLS 1.0 and TLS 1.1", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "This document specifies a new certificate type and two TLS extensions for exchanging raw public keys in Transport Layer Security (TLS) and Datagram Transport Layer Security (DTLS).  The new certificate type allows raw public keys to be used for authentication.", "ad": "/api/v1/person/person/19483/", "expires": "2014-07-24T20:34:11Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 41052, "intended_std_level": "/api/v1/name/intendedstdlevelname/ps/", "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-oob-pubkey", "note": "Joe Salowey (jsalowey@cisco.com) is the Document Shepherd", "notify": "", "pages": 18, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-oob-pubkey/", "rev": "11", "rfc": null, "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": "/api/v1/person/email/joe@salowey.net/", "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/3/", "/api/v1/doc/state/108/", "/api/v1/doc/state/115/", "/api/v1/doc/state/7/", "/api/v1/doc/state/38/"], "std_level": "/api/v1/name/stdlevelname/ps/", "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "submissions": ["/api/v1/submit/submission/38048/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/38349/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/39880/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/40980/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/43272/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/45885/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/45902/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/48261/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/52928/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/53088/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/54860/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/56987/"], "tags": [], "time": "2017-05-11T07:10:56Z", "title": "Using Raw Public Keys in Transport Layer Security (TLS) and Datagram Transport Layer Security (DTLS)", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": 4628}, {"abstract": "This document builds upon the TLS Protocol Specification [TLS].  The\r\nextensions described herein are intended to apply to Version 1.0 of\r\nthe TLS specification.\r\nThe purpose of this document is to update the TLS protocol with\r\nextensions to support the certificates, public key algorithms,\r\nsymmetric ciphers, hash algorithms, and trust model used by OpenPGP\r\n[OpenPGP].\r\n\r\n   This document uses the same notation used in the TLS Protocol draft.", "ad": null, "expires": "2002-08-23T07:00:02Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 22008, "intended_std_level": null, "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-openpgp", "note": "", "notify": "", "pages": 4, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-openpgp/", "rev": "02", "rfc": null, "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": null, "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/2/", "/api/v1/doc/state/150/", "/api/v1/doc/state/38/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "submissions": [], "tags": [], "time": "2002-02-19T08:00:00Z", "title": "Extensions to TLS for OpenPGP keys", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": 987}, {"abstract": "This memo proposes extensions to the Transport Layer Security (TLS) protocol to support the OpenPGP key format.  The extensions discussed here include a certificate type negotiation mechanism, and the required modifications to the TLS Handshake Protocol.  This memo defines an Experimental Protocol for the Internet community.", "ad": "/api/v1/person/person/5376/", "expires": "2007-03-02T00:28:21Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 25445, "intended_std_level": "/api/v1/name/intendedstdlevelname/exp/", "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-openpgp-keys", "note": "", "notify": "", "pages": 8, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-openpgp-keys/", "rev": "11", "rfc": null, "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": null, "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/3/", "/api/v1/doc/state/107/", "/api/v1/doc/state/7/"], "std_level": "/api/v1/name/stdlevelname/exp/", "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "submissions": [], "tags": ["/api/v1/name/doctagname/app-min/"], "time": "2015-10-14T20:50:26Z", "title": "Using OpenPGP Keys for Transport Layer Security (TLS) Authentication", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": 1851}, {"abstract": "This memo describes a Transport Layer Security (TLS) extension that can be used to pad ClientHello messages to a desired size.", "ad": "/api/v1/person/person/19177/", "expires": "2016-03-11T22:13:53Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 59177, "intended_std_level": "/api/v1/name/intendedstdlevelname/ps/", "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-padding", "note": "", "notify": "", "pages": 4, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-padding/", "rev": "04", "rfc": null, "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": "/api/v1/person/email/jsalowey@tableau.com/", "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/3/", "/api/v1/doc/state/108/", "/api/v1/doc/state/115/", "/api/v1/doc/state/7/", "/api/v1/doc/state/44/"], "std_level": "/api/v1/name/stdlevelname/ps/", "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "submissions": ["/api/v1/submit/submission/66146/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/66755/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/71684/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/71853/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/71970/"], "tags": [], "time": "2015-10-21T21:07:24Z", "title": "A Transport Layer Security (TLS) ClientHello Padding Extension", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": 1060}, {"abstract": "   The pre-shared key mechanism available in TLS 1.3 is not suitable for\n   usage with low-entropy keys, such as passwords entered by users.\n   This document describes an extension that enables the use of\n   password-authenticated key exchange protocols with TLS 1.3.\n", "ad": null, "expires": "2027-01-07T22:47:29Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 149466, "intended_std_level": null, "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-pake", "note": "", "notify": "", "pages": 29, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-pake/", "rev": "02", "rfc": null, "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": null, "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/1/", "/api/v1/doc/state/150/", "/api/v1/doc/state/38/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "submissions": ["/api/v1/submit/submission/155072/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/160816/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/166278/"], "tags": [], "time": "2026-07-06T22:47:29Z", "title": "A Password Authenticated Key Exchange Extension for TLS 1.3", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "This document presents a shared-key authentication mechanism for the TLS protocol.  It is intended to allow TLS clients to authenticate using a secret key (such as a password) shared with either the server or a third-party authentication service.  The security of the secret authentication key is augmented by its integration into the normal SSL/TLS server authentication/key exchange mechanism.", "ad": null, "expires": "1997-05-26T07:00:00Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 18787, "intended_std_level": null, "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-passauth", "note": "", "notify": "", "pages": 5, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-passauth/", "rev": "00", "rfc": null, "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": null, "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/2/", "/api/v1/doc/state/150/", "/api/v1/doc/state/38/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "submissions": [], "tags": [], "time": "1996-11-22T08:00:00Z", "title": "Addition of Shared Key Authentication to Transport Layer Security (TLS)", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": 2296}, {"abstract": "The TLS Pathsec Protocol (or Pathsec Protocol in short) extends the\r\nTLS protocol into securing data in transit not only between two end\r\npoints, but also between the intermediaries en route, based on TLS\r\n1.0 with appropriate extensions that include injecting source routing\r\npolicies above the Transport layer.\r\n\r\n", "ad": null, "expires": "2002-04-04T08:00:00Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 24922, "intended_std_level": null, "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-pathsec", "note": "", "notify": "", "pages": 50, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-pathsec/", "rev": "00", "rfc": null, "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": null, "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/2/", "/api/v1/doc/state/150/", "/api/v1/doc/state/38/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "submissions": [], "tags": [], "time": "2001-10-05T07:00:00Z", "title": "TLS Pathsec Protocol\r\n", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": 9943}, {"abstract": "This document requires that Transport Layer Security (TLS) clients and servers never negotiate the use of RC4 cipher suites when they establish connections.  This applies to all TLS versions.  This document updates RFCs 5246, 4346, and 2246.", "ad": "/api/v1/person/person/19177/", "expires": "2015-04-04T23:12:52Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 56388, "intended_std_level": "/api/v1/name/intendedstdlevelname/ps/", "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-prohibiting-rc4", "note": "", "notify": "", "pages": 6, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-prohibiting-rc4/", "rev": "01", "rfc": null, "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": "/api/v1/person/email/joe@salowey.net/", "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/3/", "/api/v1/doc/state/110/", "/api/v1/doc/state/113/", "/api/v1/doc/state/7/", "/api/v1/doc/state/44/"], "std_level": "/api/v1/name/stdlevelname/ps/", "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "submissions": ["/api/v1/submit/submission/61880/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/63254/"], "tags": [], "time": "2015-10-14T20:53:08Z", "title": "Prohibiting RC4 Cipher Suites", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": 1114}, {"abstract": "This document specifies Version 1.0 of the Transport Layer Security (TLS) protocol.  The TLS protocol provides communications privacy over the Internet.  The protocol allows client/server applications to communicate in a way that is designed to prevent eavesdropping, tampering, or message forgery.", "ad": null, "expires": "1999-05-16T07:00:06Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 18866, "intended_std_level": "/api/v1/name/intendedstdlevelname/ps/", "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-protocol", "note": "", "notify": "", "pages": 80, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-protocol/", "rev": "06", "rfc": null, "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": null, "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/3/", "/api/v1/doc/state/150/"], "std_level": "/api/v1/name/stdlevelname/hist/", "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "submissions": [], "tags": [], "time": "2021-02-02T08:26:08Z", "title": "The TLS Protocol Version 1.0", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": 20621}, {"abstract": "This document specifies three sets of new ciphersuites for the Transport Layer Security (TLS) protocol to support authentication based on pre-shared keys (PSKs).  These pre-shared keys are symmetric keys, shared in advance among the communicating parties.  The first set of ciphersuites uses only symmetric key operations for authentication.  The second set uses a Diffie-Hellman exchange authenticated with a pre-shared key, and the third set combines public key authentication of the server with pre-shared key authentication of the client. [STANDARDS-TRACK]", "ad": "/api/v1/person/person/5376/", "expires": "2005-12-24T19:44:51Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 28853, "intended_std_level": "/api/v1/name/intendedstdlevelname/ps/", "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-psk", "note": "", "notify": "ekr@networkresonance.com", "pages": 15, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-psk/", "rev": "09", "rfc": null, "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": null, "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/3/", "/api/v1/doc/state/7/"], "std_level": "/api/v1/name/stdlevelname/ps/", "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "submissions": [], "tags": ["/api/v1/name/doctagname/app-min/"], "time": "2015-10-14T20:50:59Z", "title": "Pre-Shared Key Ciphersuites for Transport Layer Security (TLS)", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": 3818}, {"abstract": "RFC 4279 and RFC 4785 describe pre-shared key cipher suites for Transport Layer Security (TLS).  However, all those cipher suites use SHA-1 in their Message Authentication Code (MAC) algorithm.  This document describes a set of pre-shared key cipher suites for TLS that uses stronger digest algorithms (i.e., SHA-256 or SHA-384) and another set that uses the Advanced Encryption Standard (AES) in Galois Counter Mode (GCM). [STANDARDS-TRACK]", "ad": "/api/v1/person/person/106164/", "expires": "2009-05-03T07:00:05Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 35620, "intended_std_level": "/api/v1/name/intendedstdlevelname/ps/", "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-psk-new-mac-aes-gcm", "note": "", "notify": "", "pages": 7, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-psk-new-mac-aes-gcm/", "rev": "05", "rfc": null, "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": null, "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/3/", "/api/v1/doc/state/108/", "/api/v1/doc/state/7/"], "std_level": "/api/v1/name/stdlevelname/ps/", "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "submissions": ["/api/v1/submit/submission/7072/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/9410/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/9431/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/10280/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/10330/"], "tags": ["/api/v1/name/doctagname/app-min/"], "time": "2015-10-14T20:51:55Z", "title": "Pre-Shared Key Cipher Suites for TLS with SHA-256/384 and AES Galois Counter Mode", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": 1943}, {"abstract": "This document specifies authentication-only ciphersuites (with no encryption) for the Pre-Shared Key (PSK) based Transport Layer Security (TLS) protocol.  These ciphersuites are useful when authentication and integrity protection is desired, but confidentiality is not needed or not permitted. [STANDARDS-TRACK]", "ad": "/api/v1/person/person/5376/", "expires": "2007-04-25T23:38:04Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 33044, "intended_std_level": "/api/v1/name/intendedstdlevelname/ps/", "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-psk-null", "note": "", "notify": "", "pages": 5, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-psk-null/", "rev": "03", "rfc": null, "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": null, "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/3/", "/api/v1/doc/state/107/", "/api/v1/doc/state/7/"], "std_level": "/api/v1/name/stdlevelname/ps/", "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "submissions": [], "tags": ["/api/v1/name/doctagname/app-min/"], "time": "2015-10-14T20:51:34Z", "title": "Pre-Shared Key (PSK) Ciphersuites with NULL Encryption for Transport Layer Security (TLS)", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": 1163}, {"abstract": "   This memo defines several new ciphersuites for the Transport Layer\n   Security (TLS) protocol to support certificate-less, secure\n   authentication using only a simple, low-entropy, password.  The\n   ciphersuites are all based on an authentication and key exchange\n   protocol that is resistant to off-line dictionary attack.\n", "ad": null, "expires": "2016-08-29T06:30:02Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 50038, "intended_std_level": null, "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-pwd", "note": "", "notify": "", "pages": 36, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-pwd/", "rev": "07", "rfc": null, "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": null, "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/4/", "/api/v1/doc/state/150/", "/api/v1/doc/state/39/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "submissions": ["/api/v1/submit/submission/47652/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/53343/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/55961/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/56352/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/59023/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/63093/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/68062/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/76002/"], "tags": ["/api/v1/name/doctagname/other/"], "time": "2016-06-22T18:14:23Z", "title": "Secure Password Ciphersuites for Transport Layer Security (TLS)", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": 11418}, {"abstract": "An extension to Transport Layer Security (TLS) is defined that allows endpoints to negotiate the maximum size of protected records that each will send the other.\n\n This replaces the maximum fragment length extension defined in RFC 6066.", "ad": "/api/v1/person/person/115214/", "expires": "2018-11-19T01:58:20Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 79839, "intended_std_level": "/api/v1/name/intendedstdlevelname/ps/", "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-record-limit", "note": "", "notify": "Sean Turner <sean@sn3rd.com>", "pages": 8, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-record-limit/", "rev": "03", "rfc": null, "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": "/api/v1/person/email/sean@sn3rd.com/", "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/3/", "/api/v1/doc/state/108/", "/api/v1/doc/state/112/", "/api/v1/doc/state/7/", "/api/v1/doc/state/44/"], "std_level": "/api/v1/name/stdlevelname/ps/", "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "submissions": ["/api/v1/submit/submission/89015/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/89210/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/92902/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/95329/"], "tags": [], "time": "2018-12-19T15:06:24Z", "title": "Record Size Limit Extension for TLS", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "Secure Socket Layer (SSL) and Transport Layer Security (TLS) renegotiation are vulnerable to an attack in which the attacker forms a TLS connection with the target server, injects content of his choice, and then splices in a new TLS connection from a client.  The server treats the client's initial TLS handshake as a renegotiation and thus believes that the initial data transmitted by the attacker is from the same entity as the subsequent client data.  This specification defines a TLS extension to cryptographically tie renegotiations to the TLS connections they are being performed over, thus preventing this attack. [STANDARDS-TRACK]", "ad": "/api/v1/person/person/106164/", "expires": "2010-07-09T22:26:32Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 38234, "intended_std_level": "/api/v1/name/intendedstdlevelname/ps/", "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-renegotiation", "note": "", "notify": "", "pages": 15, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-renegotiation/", "rev": "03", "rfc": null, "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": null, "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/3/", "/api/v1/doc/state/108/", "/api/v1/doc/state/7/"], "std_level": "/api/v1/name/stdlevelname/ps/", "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "submissions": ["/api/v1/submit/submission/19873/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/19745/"], "tags": ["/api/v1/name/doctagname/app-min/"], "time": "2015-10-14T20:52:14Z", "title": "Transport Layer Security (TLS) Renegotiation Indication Extension", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": 4287}, {"abstract": "This document specifies Version 1.1 of the Transport Layer Security (TLS) protocol.  The TLS protocol provides communications security over the Internet.  The protocol allows client/server applications to communicate in a way that is designed to prevent eavesdropping, tampering, or message forgery.", "ad": "/api/v1/person/person/5376/", "expires": "2005-12-25T19:42:15Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 25556, "intended_std_level": "/api/v1/name/intendedstdlevelname/ps/", "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-rfc2246-bis", "note": "", "notify": "", "pages": 87, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-rfc2246-bis/", "rev": "13", "rfc": null, "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": null, "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/3/", "/api/v1/doc/state/7/"], "std_level": "/api/v1/name/stdlevelname/hist/", "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "submissions": [], "tags": ["/api/v1/name/doctagname/app-min/"], "time": "2021-02-02T08:27:00Z", "title": "The Transport Layer Security (TLS) Protocol Version 1.1", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": 22058}, {"abstract": "This document describes extensions that may be used to add functionality to Transport Layer Security (TLS). It provides both generic extension mechanisms for the TLS handshake client and server hellos, and specific extensions using these generic mechanisms.\n\n The extensions may be used by TLS clients and servers. The extensions are backwards compatible: communication is possible between TLS clients that support the extensions and TLS servers that do not support the extensions, and vice versa. [STANDARDS-TRACK]", "ad": "/api/v1/person/person/5376/", "expires": "2006-04-07T16:45:23Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 30264, "intended_std_level": "/api/v1/name/intendedstdlevelname/ps/", "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-rfc3546bis", "note": "", "notify": "ekr@networkresonance.com", "pages": 30, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-rfc3546bis/", "rev": "02", "rfc": null, "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": null, "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/3/", "/api/v1/doc/state/7/"], "std_level": "/api/v1/name/stdlevelname/ps/", "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "submissions": [], "tags": ["/api/v1/name/doctagname/app-min/"], "time": "2020-07-29T07:30:28Z", "title": "Transport Layer Security (TLS) Extensions", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": 8036}, {"abstract": "This document specifies Version 1.2 of the Transport Layer Security (TLS) protocol.  The TLS protocol provides communications security over the Internet.  The protocol allows client/server applications to communicate in a way that is designed to prevent eavesdropping, tampering, or message forgery. [STANDARDS-TRACK]", "ad": "/api/v1/person/person/19790/", "expires": "2008-09-27T17:33:00Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 32366, "intended_std_level": "/api/v1/name/intendedstdlevelname/ps/", "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-rfc4346-bis", "note": "", "notify": "", "pages": 104, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-rfc4346-bis/", "rev": "10", "rfc": null, "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": null, "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/3/", "/api/v1/doc/state/108/", "/api/v1/doc/state/7/"], "std_level": "/api/v1/name/stdlevelname/ps/", "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "submissions": [], "tags": ["/api/v1/name/doctagname/app-min/"], "time": "2020-01-21T08:28:58Z", "title": "The Transport Layer Security (TLS) Protocol Version 1.2", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": 26785}, {"abstract": "This document specifies version 1.2 of the Datagram Transport Layer Security (DTLS) protocol.  The DTLS protocol provides communications privacy for datagram protocols.  The protocol allows client/server applications to communicate in a way that is designed to prevent eavesdropping, tampering, or message forgery.  The DTLS protocol is based on the Transport Layer Security (TLS) protocol and provides equivalent security guarantees.  Datagram semantics of the underlying transport are preserved by the DTLS protocol.  This document updates DTLS 1.0 to work with TLS version 1.2. [STANDARDS-TRACK]", "ad": "/api/v1/person/person/19483/", "expires": "2012-01-05T01:54:33Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 35824, "intended_std_level": "/api/v1/name/intendedstdlevelname/ps/", "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-rfc4347-bis", "note": "Joe Salowey (jsalowey@cisco.com) is the document Shepherd.", "notify": "", "pages": 32, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-rfc4347-bis/", "rev": "06", "rfc": null, "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": null, "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/3/", "/api/v1/doc/state/108/", "/api/v1/doc/state/7/", "/api/v1/doc/state/38/"], "std_level": "/api/v1/name/stdlevelname/ps/", "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "submissions": ["/api/v1/submit/submission/13574/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/18278/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/25426/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/33737/"], "tags": [], "time": "2015-10-14T20:51:57Z", "title": "Datagram Transport Layer Security Version 1.2", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": 8945}, {"abstract": "This document provides specifications for existing TLS extensions.  It is a companion document for RFC 5246, \"The Transport Layer Security (TLS) Protocol Version 1.2\".  The extensions specified are server_name, max_fragment_length, client_certificate_url, trusted_ca_keys, truncated_hmac, and status_request. [STANDARDS-TRACK]", "ad": "/api/v1/person/person/19483/", "expires": "2011-03-24T17:22:07Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 34401, "intended_std_level": "/api/v1/name/intendedstdlevelname/ps/", "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-rfc4366-bis", "note": "Document shepherd is Joe Salowey &lt;jsalowey@cisco.com&gt;", "notify": "", "pages": 25, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-rfc4366-bis/", "rev": "12", "rfc": null, "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": null, "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/3/", "/api/v1/doc/state/108/", "/api/v1/doc/state/7/"], "std_level": "/api/v1/name/stdlevelname/ps/", "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "submissions": ["/api/v1/submit/submission/23693/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/23960/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/24156/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/25655/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/26489/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/26500/"], "tags": ["/api/v1/name/doctagname/app-min/"], "time": "2020-01-21T08:31:04Z", "title": "Transport Layer Security (TLS) Extensions: Extension Definitions", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": 6875}, {"abstract": "This document describes key exchange algorithms based on Elliptic Curve Cryptography (ECC) for the Transport Layer Security (TLS) protocol. In particular, it specifies the use of Ephemeral Elliptic Curve Diffie-Hellman (ECDHE) key agreement in a TLS handshake and the use of the Elliptic Curve Digital Signature Algorithm (ECDSA) and Edwards-curve Digital Signature Algorithm (EdDSA) as authentication mechanisms.\n\n This document obsoletes RFC 4492.", "ad": "/api/v1/person/person/104851/", "expires": "2017-11-07T07:52:37Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 58741, "intended_std_level": "/api/v1/name/intendedstdlevelname/ps/", "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-rfc4492bis", "note": "", "notify": "\"Sean Turner\" <sean@sn3rd.com>", "pages": 34, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-rfc4492bis/", "rev": "17", "rfc": null, "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": "/api/v1/person/email/sean@sn3rd.com/", "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/3/", "/api/v1/doc/state/108/", "/api/v1/doc/state/115/", "/api/v1/doc/state/7/", "/api/v1/doc/state/44/"], "std_level": "/api/v1/name/stdlevelname/ps/", "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "submissions": ["/api/v1/submit/submission/65119/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/67742/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/65867/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/70640/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/73363/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/73907/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/75493/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/77214/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/79840/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/82123/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/83725/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/83726/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/84341/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/84649/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/84754/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/85427/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/85604/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/86434/"], "tags": [], "time": "2020-01-21T08:34:42Z", "title": "Elliptic Curve Cryptography (ECC) Cipher Suites for Transport Layer Security (TLS) Versions 1.2 and Earlier", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": 8794}, {"abstract": "   This document specifies Version 1.3 of the Transport Layer Security\n   (TLS) protocol.  The TLS protocol provides communications security\n   over the Internet.  The protocol allows client/server applications to\n   communicate in a way that is designed to prevent eavesdropping,\n   tampering, or message forgery.\n", "ad": null, "expires": "2014-10-19T21:30:27Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 55250, "intended_std_level": null, "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-rfc5246-bis", "note": "", "notify": "", "pages": 102, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-rfc5246-bis/", "rev": "00", "rfc": null, "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": null, "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/4/", "/api/v1/doc/state/150/", "/api/v1/doc/state/40/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "submissions": ["/api/v1/submit/submission/59396/"], "tags": ["/api/v1/name/doctagname/other/"], "time": "2014-04-17T21:30:27Z", "title": "The Transport Layer Security (TLS) Protocol Version 1.3", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": 27594}, {"abstract": "   This document specifies version 1.3 of the Transport Layer Security\n   (TLS) protocol.  TLS allows client/server applications to communicate\n   over the Internet in a way that is designed to prevent eavesdropping,\n   tampering, and message forgery.\n\n   This document updates RFCs 5705, 6066, 7627, and 8422 and obsoletes\n   RFCs 5077, 5246, 6961, 8422, and 8446.  This document also specifies\n   new requirements for TLS 1.2 implementations.\n", "ad": "/api/v1/person/person/112723/", "expires": "2026-03-17T15:16:00Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 98530, "intended_std_level": "/api/v1/name/intendedstdlevelname/ps/", "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-rfc8446bis", "note": "", "notify": "sean@sn3rd.com", "pages": 161, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-rfc8446bis/", "rev": "14", "rfc": null, "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": "/api/v1/person/email/sean@sn3rd.com/", "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/3/", "/api/v1/doc/state/108/", "/api/v1/doc/state/112/", "/api/v1/doc/state/7/", "/api/v1/doc/state/44/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "submissions": ["/api/v1/submit/submission/114763/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/117437/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/122508/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/121051/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/125125/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/129786/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/132676/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/132876/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/134958/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/134959/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/140842/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/145627/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/149274/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/154164/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/155266/"], "tags": [], "time": "2026-07-11T16:03:48Z", "title": "The Transport Layer Security (TLS) Protocol Version 1.3", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "   This document updates the changes to TLS and DTLS IANA registries\n   made in RFC 8447.  It adds a new value \"D\" for discouraged to the\n   Recommended column of the selected TLS registries and adds a\n   \"Comment\" column to all active registries that do not already have a\n   \"Comment\" column.  Finally, it updates the registration request\n   instructions.\n\n   This document updates RFC 8447.\n", "ad": "/api/v1/person/person/112723/", "expires": "2026-01-22T07:55:07Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 107804, "intended_std_level": "/api/v1/name/intendedstdlevelname/ps/", "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-rfc8447bis", "note": "", "notify": "durumcrustulum@gmail.com", "pages": 17, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-rfc8447bis/", "rev": "15", "rfc": null, "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": "/api/v1/person/email/durumcrustulum@gmail.com/", "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/3/", "/api/v1/doc/state/108/", "/api/v1/doc/state/114/", "/api/v1/doc/state/7/", "/api/v1/doc/state/44/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "submissions": ["/api/v1/submit/submission/147217/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/125449/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/127141/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/129536/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/131338/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/132894/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/137496/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/138605/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/138606/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/139567/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/142298/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/150374/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/151209/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/152386/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/152780/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/154110/"], "tags": [], "time": "2025-12-24T18:45:19Z", "title": "IANA Registry Updates for TLS and DTLS", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "   This document specifies version 1.3 of the Datagram Transport Layer\n   Security (DTLS) protocol.  DTLS 1.3 allows client/server applications\n   to communicate over the Internet in a way that is designed to prevent\n   eavesdropping, tampering, and message forgery.\n\n   The DTLS 1.3 protocol is based on the Transport Layer Security (TLS)\n   1.3 protocol and provides equivalent security guarantees with the\n   exception of order protection / non-replayability.  Datagram\n   semantics of the underlying transport are preserved by the DTLS\n   protocol.\n\n   This document obsoletes RFC 6347.\n", "ad": null, "expires": "2027-01-07T17:03:45Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 142329, "intended_std_level": null, "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-rfc9147bis", "note": "", "notify": "", "pages": 71, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-rfc9147bis/", "rev": "02", "rfc": null, "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": null, "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/1/", "/api/v1/doc/state/150/", "/api/v1/doc/state/38/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "submissions": ["/api/v1/submit/submission/148005/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/156870/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/166074/"], "tags": [], "time": "2026-07-06T17:03:45Z", "title": "The Datagram Transport Layer Security (DTLS) Protocol Version 1.3", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "This memo describes the use of the Advanced Encryption Standard (AES) in Galois/Counter Mode (GCM) as a Transport Layer Security (TLS) authenticated encryption operation.  GCM provides both confidentiality and data origin authentication, can be efficiently implemented in hardware for speeds of 10 gigabits per second and above, and is also well-suited to software implementations.  This memo defines TLS cipher suites that use AES-GCM with RSA, DSA, and Diffie-Hellman-based key exchange mechanisms. [STANDARDS-TRACK]", "ad": "/api/v1/person/person/106164/", "expires": "2008-10-16T07:00:03Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 33902, "intended_std_level": "/api/v1/name/intendedstdlevelname/ps/", "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-rsa-aes-gcm", "note": "", "notify": "", "pages": 8, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-rsa-aes-gcm/", "rev": "03", "rfc": null, "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": null, "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/3/", "/api/v1/doc/state/108/", "/api/v1/doc/state/7/"], "std_level": "/api/v1/name/stdlevelname/ps/", "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "submissions": ["/api/v1/submit/submission/4209/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/4631/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/6442/"], "tags": ["/api/v1/name/doctagname/app-min/"], "time": "2020-01-21T08:29:09Z", "title": "AES Galois Counter Mode (GCM) Cipher Suites for TLS", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": 2116}, {"abstract": "This document proposes the addition of new cipher suites to the TLS\r\nprotocol 1.0 [TLS] to support SEED and HAS-160.\r\nThe SEED algorithm is 128-bit symmetric block cipher algorithm.\r\n[SEED] The HAS-160 is 160-bit secure hash function, whose block size\r\nis 512 bit. [HAS] Both algorithms are developed in Korea since 1997\r\nfor stronger communication security.  Currently, SEED is widely used\r\nand is the mandatory cipher in banking and stock applications in\r\nKorea.", "ad": null, "expires": "2001-01-15T08:00:00Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 22754, "intended_std_level": null, "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-seedhas", "note": "", "notify": "", "pages": 4, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-seedhas/", "rev": "00", "rfc": null, "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": null, "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/2/", "/api/v1/doc/state/150/", "/api/v1/doc/state/38/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "submissions": [], "tags": [], "time": "2000-07-14T07:00:00Z", "title": "TLS Extension for SEED and HAS-160", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": 625}, {"abstract": "   TLS 1.3 [RFC8446] specifies a signed Diffie-Hellman exchange modelled\n   after SIGMA [SIGMA].  This design is suitable for endpoints whose\n   certified credential is a signing key, which is the common situation\n   for current TLS servers.  This document describes a mode of TLS 1.3\n   in which one or both endpoints have a certified DH key which is used\n   to authenticate the exchange.\n\nNote to Readers\n\n   Source for this draft and an issue tracker can be found at\n   https://github.com/ekr/draft-rescorla-tls13-semistatic-dh\n   (https://github.com/ekr/draft-rescorla-tls13-semistatic-dh).\n", "ad": null, "expires": "2020-09-08T22:45:25Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 95075, "intended_std_level": null, "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-semistatic-dh", "note": "", "notify": "", "pages": 7, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-semistatic-dh/", "rev": "01", "rfc": null, "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": null, "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/2/", "/api/v1/doc/state/150/", "/api/v1/doc/state/38/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "submissions": ["/api/v1/submit/submission/109261/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/110309/"], "tags": [], "time": "2020-09-08T07:24:31Z", "title": "Semi-Static Diffie-Hellman Key Establishment for TLS 1.3", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "The Transport Layer Security (TLS) master secret is not cryptographically bound to important session parameters such as the server certificate.  Consequently, it is possible for an active attacker to set up two sessions, one with a client and another with a server, such that the master secrets on the two sessions are the same.  Thereafter, any mechanism that relies on the master secret for authentication, including session resumption, becomes vulnerable to a man-in-the-middle attack, where the attacker can simply forward messages back and forth between the client and server.  This specification defines a TLS extension that contextually binds the master secret to a log of the full handshake that computes it, thus preventing such attacks.", "ad": "/api/v1/person/person/19177/", "expires": "2016-01-06T12:14:57Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 56967, "intended_std_level": "/api/v1/name/intendedstdlevelname/ps/", "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-session-hash", "note": "", "notify": "", "pages": 15, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-session-hash/", "rev": "06", "rfc": null, "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": "/api/v1/person/email/turners@ieca.com/", "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/3/", "/api/v1/doc/state/108/", "/api/v1/doc/state/115/", "/api/v1/doc/state/7/", "/api/v1/doc/state/44/"], "std_level": "/api/v1/name/stdlevelname/ps/", "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "submissions": ["/api/v1/submit/submission/62412/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/62457/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/63333/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/64795/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/67686/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/68503/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/70419/"], "tags": [], "time": "2015-10-14T20:53:09Z", "title": "Transport Layer Security (TLS) Session Hash and Extended Master Secret Extension", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": 4399}, {"abstract": "The TLS handshake requires the use of CPU-intensive public-key algorithms with a considerable overhead in resource-constrained environments or ones such as mainframes where users are charged for CPU time.  This document describes a means of employing TLS using symmetric keys or passwords shared in advance among communicating parties.  No modifications or alterations to the TLS protocol are required for this process.", "ad": null, "expires": "2004-04-26T07:00:02Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 27700, "intended_std_level": null, "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-sharedkeys", "note": "", "notify": "", "pages": 6, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-sharedkeys/", "rev": "02", "rfc": null, "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": null, "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/2/", "/api/v1/doc/state/150/", "/api/v1/doc/state/38/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "submissions": [], "tags": [], "time": "2003-10-24T07:00:00Z", "title": "Use of Shared Keys in the TLS Protocol", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": 3507}, {"abstract": "This document describes the general problem of encrypting the Server Name Identification (SNI) TLS parameter. The proposed solutions hide a hidden service behind a fronting service, only disclosing the SNI of the fronting service to external observers. This document lists known attacks against SNI encryption, discusses the current \"HTTP co-tenancy\" solution, and presents requirements for future TLS-layer solutions.\n\n In practice, it may well be that no solution can meet every requirement and that practical solutions will have to make some compromises.", "ad": "/api/v1/person/person/115214/", "expires": "2020-04-30T21:50:48Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 79857, "intended_std_level": "/api/v1/name/intendedstdlevelname/inf/", "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-sni-encryption", "note": "", "notify": "Sean Turner <sean@sn3rd.com>, Joseph Salowey <joe@salowey.net>", "pages": 13, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-sni-encryption/", "rev": "09", "rfc": null, "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": "/api/v1/person/email/joe@salowey.net/", "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/3/", "/api/v1/doc/state/110/", "/api/v1/doc/state/113/", "/api/v1/doc/state/7/", "/api/v1/doc/state/44/"], "std_level": "/api/v1/name/stdlevelname/inf/", "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "submissions": ["/api/v1/submit/submission/89031/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/93362/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/92961/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/95359/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/99974/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/106024/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/106595/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/106693/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/106875/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/107361/"], "tags": [], "time": "2020-07-28T21:58:35Z", "title": "Issues and Requirements for Server Name Identification (SNI) Encryption in TLS", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "   An extension is defined for TLS that allows a client and server to\n   detect an attempt to force the use of less-preferred application\n   protocol even where protocol options are incompatible.  This\n   supplements application-layer protocol negotiation (ALPN), which\n   allows choices between compatible protocols to be authenticated.\n", "ad": null, "expires": "2023-01-01T08:18:38Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 104028, "intended_std_level": null, "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-snip", "note": "", "notify": "", "pages": 12, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-snip/", "rev": "02", "rfc": null, "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": null, "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/2/", "/api/v1/doc/state/150/", "/api/v1/doc/state/38/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "submissions": ["/api/v1/submit/submission/124177/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/121085/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/126920/"], "tags": [], "time": "2023-01-01T08:13:28Z", "title": "Secure Negotiation of Incompatible Protocols in TLS", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "This memo presents a technique for using the Secure Remote Password protocol as an authentication method for the Transport Layer Security protocol.  This memo provides information for the Internet community.", "ad": "/api/v1/person/person/19790/", "expires": "2007-12-16T23:25:54Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 24031, "intended_std_level": "/api/v1/name/intendedstdlevelname/inf/", "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-srp", "note": "", "notify": "ekr@networkresonance.com, Pasi.Eronen@nokia.com", "pages": 24, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-srp/", "rev": "14", "rfc": null, "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": null, "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/3/", "/api/v1/doc/state/108/", "/api/v1/doc/state/7/"], "std_level": "/api/v1/name/stdlevelname/inf/", "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "submissions": [], "tags": ["/api/v1/name/doctagname/app-min/"], "time": "2023-10-11T07:15:34Z", "title": "Using the Secure Remote Password (SRP) Protocol for TLS Authentication", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": 5722}, {"abstract": "This document describes the SSH transport layer protocol.  The protocol can be used as a basis for a number of secure network services.  It provides strong encryption, mutual authentication, and integrity protection.", "ad": null, "expires": "1996-12-16T08:00:00Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 18518, "intended_std_level": null, "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-ssh", "note": "", "notify": "", "pages": 19, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-ssh/", "rev": "00", "rfc": null, "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": null, "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/2/", "/api/v1/doc/state/150/", "/api/v1/doc/state/38/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "submissions": [], "tags": [], "time": "1996-06-14T07:00:00Z", "title": "SSH Transport Layer Protocol", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": 6550}, {"abstract": "This document recommends for several modifications be made to the SSL 3.0 protocol as it is standardized by the IETF under the name of TLS.  These changes primarily standardize various technical details of the protocol and make some other minor modifications.", "ad": null, "expires": "1997-05-31T07:00:00Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 18849, "intended_std_level": null, "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-ssl-mods", "note": "", "notify": "", "pages": 4, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-ssl-mods/", "rev": "00", "rfc": null, "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": null, "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/2/", "/api/v1/doc/state/150/", "/api/v1/doc/state/38/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "submissions": [], "tags": [], "time": "1996-11-27T08:00:00Z", "title": "Modifications to the SSL protocol for TLS", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": 1320}, {"abstract": "This document specifies Version 3.0 of the Secure Sockets Layer (SSL V3.0) protocol, a security protocol that provides communications privacy over the Internet.  The protocol allows client/server applications to communicate in a way that is designed to prevent eavesdropping, tampering, or message forgery.", "ad": null, "expires": "1997-05-25T07:00:00Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 18149, "intended_std_level": null, "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-ssl-version3", "note": "", "notify": "", "pages": 63, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-ssl-version3/", "rev": "00", "rfc": null, "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": null, "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/2/", "/api/v1/doc/state/150/", "/api/v1/doc/state/38/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "submissions": [], "tags": [], "time": "1996-11-21T08:00:00Z", "title": "The SSL Protocol Version 3.0", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": 15824}, {"abstract": "This document requires that when Transport Layer Security (TLS) clients and servers establish connections, they never negotiate the use of Secure Sockets Layer (SSL) version 2.0.  This document updates the backward compatibility sections found in the Transport Layer Security (TLS). [STANDARDS-TRACK]", "ad": "/api/v1/person/person/102154/", "expires": "2011-06-20T23:10:32Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 39052, "intended_std_level": "/api/v1/name/intendedstdlevelname/ps/", "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-ssl2-must-not", "note": "", "notify": "", "pages": 4, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-ssl2-must-not/", "rev": "04", "rfc": null, "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": null, "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/3/", "/api/v1/doc/state/110/", "/api/v1/doc/state/7/"], "std_level": "/api/v1/name/stdlevelname/ps/", "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "submissions": [], "tags": ["/api/v1/name/doctagname/app-min/"], "time": "2018-10-13T07:19:50Z", "title": "Prohibiting Secure Sockets Layer (SSL) Version 2.0", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": 959}, {"abstract": "The Secure Sockets Layer version 3.0 (SSLv3), as specified in RFC 6101, is not sufficiently secure. This document requires that SSLv3 not be used. The replacement versions, in particular, Transport Layer Security (TLS) 1.2 (RFC 5246), are considerably more secure and capable protocols.\n\n This document updates the backward compatibility section of RFC 5246 and its predecessors to prohibit fallback to SSLv3.", "ad": "/api/v1/person/person/19177/", "expires": "2015-10-12T19:46:09Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 58842, "intended_std_level": "/api/v1/name/intendedstdlevelname/ps/", "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-sslv3-diediedie", "note": "", "notify": "", "pages": 7, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-sslv3-diediedie/", "rev": "03", "rfc": null, "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": "/api/v1/person/email/joe@salowey.net/", "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/3/", "/api/v1/doc/state/110/", "/api/v1/doc/state/115/", "/api/v1/doc/state/7/", "/api/v1/doc/state/44/"], "std_level": "/api/v1/name/stdlevelname/ps/", "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "submissions": ["/api/v1/submit/submission/65145/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/67004/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/67005/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/68372/"], "tags": [], "time": "2018-12-20T08:29:27Z", "title": "Deprecating Secure Sockets Layer Version 3.0", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": 1650}, {"abstract": "The organizational separation between operators of TLS and DTLS endpoints and the certification authority can create limitations.  For example, the lifetime of certificates, how they may be used, and the algorithms they support are ultimately determined by the Certification Authority (CA).  This document describes a mechanism to overcome some of these limitations by enabling operators to delegate their own credentials for use in TLS and DTLS without breaking compatibility with peers that do not support this specification.", "ad": "/api/v1/person/person/112723/", "expires": "2023-01-01T18:17:01Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 80504, "intended_std_level": "/api/v1/name/intendedstdlevelname/ps/", "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-subcerts", "note": "", "notify": "Joseph Salowey <joe@salowey.net>", "pages": 17, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-subcerts/", "rev": "15", "rfc": null, "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": "/api/v1/person/email/joe@salowey.net/", "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/3/", "/api/v1/doc/state/108/", "/api/v1/doc/state/112/", "/api/v1/doc/state/7/", "/api/v1/doc/state/44/"], "std_level": "/api/v1/name/stdlevelname/ps/", "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "submissions": ["/api/v1/submit/submission/90874/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/96884/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/97589/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/101436/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/105400/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/107698/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/109576/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/110634/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/111661/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/112787/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/116940/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/121522/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/124974/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/126103/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/126236/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/126690/"], "tags": [], "time": "2023-07-13T22:29:44Z", "title": "Delegated Credentials for TLS and DTLS", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}]}